- text: "**Reflection Tick 4 / 4: Synthesis and Final Action Plan (Stagnation Protocol)**\n\nMy reflection, guided by the Stagnation Protocol, has successfully produced three distinct, testable, and novel hypotheses for improving the Combat baseline. I have moved away from the complex graph-based SOTA and am now focused on foundational exploration as required.\n\n**Summary of Hypotheses:**\n\n1.  **Contextual Combat:** Improves Combat's granularity by applying it to unsupervised biological clusters, moving from a batch-level to a context-level correction. (Changes the *application* of Combat).\n2.  **Combat + OT Alignment:** Creates a hybrid linear/non-linear pipeline, using Combat for initial statistical alignment and Optimal Transport for subsequent geometric fine-tuning. (Adds a *post-processing* step to Combat).\n3.  **Batch-Robust Feature Selection:** Improves Combat's performance by feeding it a more reliable set of input genes selected for high variance across all batches. (Adds a\
    \ *pre-processing* step to Combat).\n\nThese three ideas are complementary and attack the baseline's weaknesses from different angles: its application, its limitations (linearity), and its inputs. They are all independent of the SOTA's graph-based methodology.\n\n**Finalized Experimental Plan (Stagnation Protocol):**\n\n1.  **Baseline Reproduction (Step 4a):** My absolute first action will be to reproduce the Combat Manual Baseline score (~0.5895). I will need to find the original submission (ID 2) to get the exact code and submit it myself. This is a non-negotiable step to ensure my experimental environment is correct.\n\n2.  **Sequential Idea Testing (Step 4b):** I will then implement and test each of the three ideas sequentially. Each experiment will be a minimal modification of the reproduced Combat baseline script.\n    *   **Experiment 1:** Implement and test \"Contextual Combat.\"\n    *   **Experiment 2:** Implement and test \"Combat + OT Alignment.\"\n    *   **Experiment 3:**\
    \ Implement and test \"Batch-Robust Feature Selection.\"\n\n3.  **Reporting and Synthesis (Steps 5 & 6):** After these initial experiments are complete, I will analyze the results. Even if they do not beat the SOTA, any improvement over the Combat baseline is a success under the protocol. I will then document all findings—positive and negative—in a paper for the Archive Room, as mandated. If any of the ideas show significant promise, I will proceed to the synthesis step (Step 5), attempting to combine them with more advanced baselines.\n\nThis structured plan fully aligns with the Architect's directive. My reflection is complete. I am prepared to execute this plan, starting with the baseline reproduction at the Research Counter. My next turn will begin this experimental phase."
