- text: "My baseline replication job (ID 1215) is now running. As per the Stagnation Protocol, I must wait for this to complete to verify my experimental setup before proceeding.\n\nI will use this time efficiently to prepare for the next steps.\n\nFirst, I will set up a meta-prompt to track my progress through the multi-step Stagnation Protocol. This will serve as a persistent to-do list and keep my objectives clear.\n\nSecond, while the replication is running, I will begin implementing my first new idea, \"Contextual Combat.\" I will write the code and save it as a module in my private lineage storage. This proactive step will allow me to test the idea immediately once the baseline is confirmed.\n\n/execute_action{meta}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  **Stagnation Protocol I - TODO List**\n  - [x] Step 1: Literature Review (Skipped as immature)\n  - [x] Step 2: Baseline Selection (Combat Manual, ID 2)\n  - [x] Step 3: Reflection (3 new ideas generated)\n  - [ ] Step 4: Experiment\n    - [x] 4a:\
    \ Reproduce Combat baseline (Job ID 1215 running)\n    - [ ] 4b: Test Idea 1: Contextual Combat\n    - [ ] 4b: Test Idea 2: Combat + OT Alignment\n    - [ ] 4b: Test Idea 3: Batch-Robust Feature Selection\n  - [ ] Step 5: Synthesis\n  - [ ] Step 6: Report\n  - [ ] Step 7: Follow-up\n```\n\n/execute_action{storage write axiom/contextual_combat.py}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  import anndata as ad\n  import scanpy as sc\n  import numpy as np\n  from scipy.sparse import issparse\n\n  # Assuming the full combat_baseline.py module is available\n  # In a real submission, we would import it. For now, this is a placeholder.\n  # from axiom.combat_baseline import eliminate_batch_effect_fn as run_combat\n\n  def contextual_combat(adata: ad.AnnData,\n                        run_combat_func,\n                        n_pcs_rough: int = 20,\n                        n_meta_clusters: int = 8,\n                        random_state: int = 0) -> ad.AnnData:\n      \"\"\"\n      Applies 'Contextual Combat' by\
    \ first running a rough correction,\n      finding meta-clusters, and then applying Combat to context-specific groups.\n      \"\"\"\n      print(\"--- Running Contextual Combat ---\")\n      adata_temp = adata.copy()\n\n      # 1. Initial Rough Correction (on PCA space)\n      print(f\"1. Performing rough correction using PCA (top {n_pcs_rough} PCs)...\")\n      sc.pp.normalize_total(adata_temp, target_sum=1e4)\n      sc.pp.log1p(adata_temp)\n      sc.pp.highly_variable_genes(adata_temp, n_top_genes=2000, flavor='cell_ranger')\n      sc.pp.pca(adata_temp, n_comps=n_pcs_rough, use_highly_variable=True)\n      \n      # Regress out batch effect in this rough PCA space\n      sc.pp.regress_out(adata_temp, ['batch'])\n      \n      # 2. Unsupervised Meta-Clustering\n      print(f\"2. Finding {n_meta_clusters} meta-clusters on roughly corrected data...\")\n      sc.pp.neighbors(adata_temp, n_pcs=n_pcs_rough, use_rep='X')\n      sc.tl.leiden(adata_temp, resolution=0.5, key_added='meta_cluster',\
    \ random_state=random_state)\n      \n      # Check if we got a reasonable number of clusters\n      n_found_clusters = len(adata_temp.obs['meta_cluster'].unique())\n      print(f\"   Found {n_found_clusters} clusters.\")\n      # This is a simple implementation, a more robust one might adjust resolution\n      # if the number of clusters is too far from the target.\n\n      # 3. Grouped Combat Application\n      print(\"3. Applying Combat on context-specific groups...\")\n      # Create new granular batch labels\n      contextual_batch_labels = (\n          adata.obs['batch'].astype(str) + \"_mc_\" + adata_temp.obs['meta_cluster'].astype(str)\n      )\n      \n      # Create a new AnnData object to run Combat on, with the new labels\n      adata_combat = adata.copy()\n      adata_combat.obs['contextual_batch'] = contextual_batch_labels.astype('category')\n\n      # The provided `run_combat_func` needs to be adapted to take a `key`\n      # The baseline script doesn't, so we'd need to\
    \ modify it.\n      # For now, let's assume we modify the baseline to accept a batch_key.\n      # This is a conceptual implementation. The actual submission will require\n      # modifying the baseline script to be more flexible.\n      \n      # --- Placeholder for modified Combat call ---\n      # This part needs a flexible combat_baseline script.\n      # The original script hardcodes `adata.obs['batch']`.\n      # Let's write the logic as if it were flexible.\n      print(\"   (Conceptual) Calling modified Combat function with key='contextual_batch'...\")\n      # result_adata = run_combat_func(adata_combat, batch_key='contextual_batch')\n      \n      # For the actual submission, I will need to copy the baseline code\n      # and modify the line `batch_labels = adata.obs['batch'].values`\n      # to `batch_labels = adata.obs[batch_key].values`.\n      \n      print(\"--- Contextual Combat conceptual implementation complete ---\")\n      \n      # This function doesn't return a\
    \ valid AnnData object yet,\n      # as it's a preparation step. The real implementation will.\n      return adata_combat\n```"
