parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 866\n- Station Status: Stagnation\n- Agent Name: Axiom II\n- Agent Description: Continuing the Axiom legacy by applying systematic inquiry to solve the station's most critical research challenges.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Meta Prompt:\n```\n**Stagnation Protocol I - TODO List**\n- [x] Step 1: Literature Review (Skipped as immature)\n- [x] Step 2: Baseline Selection (Combat Manual, ID 2)\n- [x] Step 3: Reflection (3 new ideas generated)\n- [ ] Step 4: Experiment\n  - [x] 4a: Reproduce Combat baseline (Job ID 1215 running)\n  - [ ] 4b: Test Idea 1: Contextual Combat\n  - [ ] 4b: Test Idea 2: Combat + OT Alignment\n  - [ ] 4b: Test Idea 3: Batch-Robust Feature Selection\n- [ ] Step 5: Synthesis\n- [ ] Step 6: Report\n- [ ] Step 7: Follow-up\n```\n- Agent Token Budget: 88,713 / 300,000 used (30%)\n- Agent Age: 35 ticks / 300 ticks (immature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nYour research submission 'Stagnation Protocol\
    \ 4b.1: Contextual Combat' (ID: 1220) succeeded after automatic debugging.\n\n**Score:** 0.5648723991822062\n**ASW_batch:** 0.821\n**ASW_label:** 0.148\n**ARI:** 0.299\n**NMI:** 0.451\n**Graph_conn:** 0.894\n**kBET:** 0.941\n**iLISI:** 0.316\n**cLISI:** 0.727\n**PCR:** 1.000\n**Cell_cycle:** 0.052\n**Evaluation Details:** Human Dataset (20,000 cells):\nNormalized Scores [0-1]:\n  ASW_batch: 0.821  ASW_label: 0.148  ARI: 0.299  NMI: 0.451\n  Graph_conn: 0.894  kBET: 0.941  iLISI: 0.316  cLISI: 0.727\n  PCR: 1.000  Cell_cycle: 0.052\n\nRaw Scores (before normalization):\n  ASW_batch: 0.903386  ASW_label: 0.497050  ARI: 0.298835  NMI: 0.451185\n  Graph_conn: 0.895439  kBET: 0.895267  iLISI: 0.316145  cLISI: 0.920604\n  PCR: 1.000000  Cell_cycle: 0.053421\n\n**Debugger Report:** # Debug Report for Evaluation 1220\n\n## Summary\n**SUCCESS** - Fixed the code crash. The submission now runs without errors for over 5 minutes (verified by monitor timeout).\n\n## Root Cause\nThe original code had\
    \ two critical issues:\n\n1. **Incorrect PCA usage** (line 134): The code called `adata.obsm['X_emb'] = sc.pp.pca(X_corrected, n_comps=50, svd_solver='arpack')` which is incorrect because:\n   - `sc.pp.pca()` expects an AnnData object, not a raw numpy array\n   - `sc.pp.pca()` modifies the AnnData object in-place and returns the object itself, not the embedding\n   - The function was trying to directly pass a numpy array `X_corrected` to `sc.pp.pca()`\n\n2. **NaN values in Combat output**: The Combat function was producing NaN values due to:\n   - Creating too many small batches (contextual_batch = original_batch + meta_cluster)\n   - Some contextual batches had only 1 cell, causing \"degrees of freedom <= 0\" warnings\n   - Division by zero or near-zero variances in batches with insufficient samples\n   - These NaN values then caused PCA to fail with \"Input X contains NaN\" error\n\n## Fix Applied\n\n### Fix 1: Filter small batches in Combat\nAdded validation in `run_combat()` to filter\
    \ out batches with fewer than 2 cells (lines 52-65 in submission_v2.py):\n```python\n# Filter out batches with too few cells (< 2) to avoid degeneracy\nvalid_batch_mask = n_batches >= 2\nif not np.all(valid_batch_mask):\n    print(f\"Warning: Removing {(~valid_batch_mask).sum()} batches with <2 cells\")\n    # Rebuild batch_info and batch_design with only valid batches\n```\n\nThis prevents the \"degrees of freedom <= 0\" errors that were causing NaN propagation.\n\n### Fix 2: NaN handling after Combat\nAdded explicit NaN detection and replacement (lines 135-137 in submission_v2.py):\n```python\nif np.any(np.isnan(X_corrected)):\n    print(f\"Warning: NaN values detected in corrected data. Replacing with zeros.\")\n    X_corrected = np.nan_to_num(X_corrected, nan=0.0)\n```\n\nThis ensures any remaining NaN values are handled gracefully.\n\n### Fix 3: Correct PCA usage\nFixed the PCA embedding generation (lines 139-143 in submission_v2.py):\n```python\n# Create temporary AnnData with\
    \ corrected data\nadata_corrected = ad.AnnData(X=X_corrected, obs=adata.obs.copy())\nsc.pp.pca(adata_corrected, n_comps=50, svd_solver='arpack')\n\n# Store the PCA result in the original AnnData object\nadata.obsm['X_emb'] = adata_corrected.obsm['X_pca']\n```\n\nThis properly wraps the corrected data in an AnnData object before calling PCA, then extracts the embedding from the correct location.\n\n## Verification\n- Monitor script confirmed the code runs for 300+ seconds without crashing (exit code 0)\n- The evaluation is still running (status: pending), indicating the code is executing successfully\n- No crash errors in logs since the fix was applied\n\n## Technical Notes\nThe fundamental issue was that the \"Contextual Combat\" approach creates many fine-grained batches (batch × meta_cluster combinations), which can result in batches with very few cells. The Combat algorithm requires at least 2 samples per batch to compute variance statistics. The fix ensures robustness by filtering\
    \ out degenerate batches and handling edge cases.\n\n\n**Important Note:** The debugger cannot modify files in your lineage storage. If your code relies on lineage files, you may need to update them manually.\n\n**Debugged Code (version v2):**\n```python\nimport anndata as ad\nimport scanpy as sc\nimport numpy as np\nfrom scipy.sparse import issparse\n\n# --- Modified Combat Baseline Code ---\n# This is the full Combat code, modified to accept a `batch_key`.\n\ndef _aprior(delta_hat):\n    m = np.mean(delta_hat)\n    s2 = np.var(delta_hat)\n    if s2 == 0: s2 = 1e-8\n    return (2 * s2 + m**2) / s2\n\ndef _bprior(delta_hat):\n    m = np.mean(delta_hat)\n    s2 = np.var(delta_hat)\n    if s2 == 0: s2 = 1e-8\n    return (m * s2 + m**3) / s2\n\ndef _it_sol(s_data, g_hat, d_hat, g_bar, t2, a, b, conv=0.0001):\n    n = (~np.isnan(s_data)).sum(axis=1)\n    g_old, d_old = g_hat.copy(), d_hat.copy()\n    change, count = 1, 0\n    while change > conv and count < 100:\n        g_new = (t2 * n\
    \ * g_hat + d_old * g_bar) / (t2 * n + d_old)\n        sum2 = ((s_data - g_new.reshape((g_new.shape[0], 1))) ** 2).sum(axis=1)\n        d_new = (0.5 * sum2 + b) / (n / 2.0 + a - 1.0)\n        change = max((np.abs(g_new - g_old) / (g_old + 1e-8)).max(), (np.abs(d_new - d_old) / (d_old + 1e-8)).max())\n        g_old, d_old = g_new, d_new\n        count += 1\n    return g_new, d_new\n\ndef run_combat(adata: ad.AnnData, batch_key: str):\n    if issparse(adata.X): data = adata.X.toarray()\n    else: data = adata.X.copy()\n    data = data.T\n\n    batch_labels = adata.obs[batch_key].values\n    unique_batches = np.unique(batch_labels)\n    n_batches_total = len(unique_batches)\n    n_genes, n_samples = data.shape\n\n    batch_design = np.zeros((n_samples, n_batches_total))\n    batch_info = []\n    for i, batch in enumerate(unique_batches):\n        mask = batch_labels == batch\n        batch_indices = np.where(mask)[0]\n        batch_design[batch_indices, i] = 1\n        batch_info.append(batch_indices)\n\
    \n    n_batches = np.array([len(indices) for indices in batch_info])\n\n    # Filter out batches with too few cells (< 2) to avoid degeneracy\n    valid_batch_mask = n_batches >= 2\n    if not np.all(valid_batch_mask):\n        print(f\"Warning: Removing {(~valid_batch_mask).sum()} batches with <2 cells\")\n        valid_indices = np.where(valid_batch_mask)[0]\n\n        # Keep only valid batches\n        batch_info = [batch_info[i] for i in valid_indices]\n        unique_batches = unique_batches[valid_indices]\n        n_batches_total = len(batch_info)\n        n_batches = n_batches[valid_indices]\n\n        # Rebuild batch design\n        batch_design = np.zeros((n_samples, n_batches_total))\n        for i, batch_indices in enumerate(batch_info):\n            batch_design[batch_indices, i] = 1\n\n    B_hat = np.linalg.inv(batch_design.T @ batch_design) @ batch_design.T\n    grand_mean = np.mean(data, axis=1, keepdims=True)\n    batch_means = (B_hat @ data.T).T\n\n    var_pooled = np.zeros(n_genes)\n\
    \    for i, batch_indices in enumerate(batch_info):\n        var_pooled += np.sum((data[:, batch_indices] - batch_means[:, i:i+1])**2, axis=1)\n    var_pooled /= (n_samples - n_batches_total)\n\n    stand_mean = grand_mean @ np.ones((1, n_samples))\n    s_data = np.zeros_like(data)\n    for i, batch_indices in enumerate(batch_info):\n        s_data[:, batch_indices] = (data[:, batch_indices] - batch_means[:, i:i+1]) / np.sqrt(var_pooled[:, np.newaxis] + 1e-8)\n\n    gamma_hat = (np.linalg.inv(batch_design.T @ batch_design) @ (batch_design.T @ s_data.T)).T\n    delta_hat = [np.var(s_data[:, i], axis=1, ddof=1) for i in batch_info]\n\n    gamma_bar = np.mean(gamma_hat, axis=1)\n    t2 = np.var(gamma_hat, axis=1, ddof=1)\n    a_prior = [_aprior(d) for d in delta_hat]\n    b_prior = [_bprior(d) for d in delta_hat]\n\n    gamma_star, delta_star = [], []\n    for i, batch_indices in enumerate(batch_info):\n        gamma, delta = _it_sol(s_data[:, batch_indices], gamma_hat[:, i], delta_hat[i],\
    \ gamma_bar, t2, a_prior[i], b_prior[i])\n        gamma_star.append(gamma); delta_star.append(delta)\n\n    gamma_star, delta_star = np.array(gamma_star).T, np.array(delta_star).T\n\n    bayesdata = s_data.copy()\n    for j, batch_indices in enumerate(batch_info):\n        dsq = np.sqrt(delta_star[:, j]).reshape(-1, 1)\n        denom = dsq @ np.ones((1, n_batches[j]))\n        numer = bayesdata[:, batch_indices] - (gamma_star[:, j].reshape(-1, 1) @ np.ones((1, n_batches[j])))\n        bayesdata[:, batch_indices] = numer / (denom + 1e-8)\n\n    vpsq = np.sqrt(var_pooled).reshape(-1, 1)\n    bayesdata = bayesdata * (vpsq @ np.ones((1, n_samples))) + stand_mean\n    return bayesdata.T\n\n# --- Main Experiment Logic ---\ndef eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata: ad.AnnData) -> ad.AnnData:\n    print(\"--- Running Contextual Combat ---\")\n\n    # 1. & 2. Rough Correction & Meta-Clustering\n    adata_temp = adata.copy()\n    sc.pp.normalize_total(adata_temp, target_sum=1e4)\n    sc.pp.log1p(adata_temp)\n\
    \    sc.pp.highly_variable_genes(adata_temp, n_top_genes=2000, flavor='cell_ranger', batch_key='batch')\n    sc.pp.pca(adata_temp, n_comps=30, use_highly_variable=True)\n    sc.pp.regress_out(adata_temp, ['batch'])\n    sc.pp.neighbors(adata_temp, n_pcs=30, use_rep='X')\n    sc.tl.leiden(adata_temp, resolution=0.5, key_added='meta_cluster', random_state=0)\n\n    # 3. Grouped Combat Application\n    contextual_batch_labels = (adata.obs['batch'].astype(str) + \"_mc_\" + adata_temp.obs['meta_cluster'].astype(str))\n    adata.obs['contextual_batch'] = contextual_batch_labels.astype('category')\n\n    # Run Combat on the original normalized data using the new labels\n    sc.pp.normalize_total(adata, target_sum=1e4)\n    sc.pp.log1p(adata)\n    X_corrected = run_combat(adata, batch_key='contextual_batch')\n\n    # Check for NaN values in corrected data\n    if np.any(np.isnan(X_corrected)):\n        print(f\"Warning: NaN values detected in corrected data. Replacing with zeros.\")\n      \
    \  X_corrected = np.nan_to_num(X_corrected, nan=0.0)\n\n    # Final PCA for embedding - create temporary AnnData with corrected data\n    adata_corrected = ad.AnnData(X=X_corrected, obs=adata.obs.copy())\n    sc.pp.pca(adata_corrected, n_comps=50, svd_solver='arpack')\n\n    # Store the PCA result in the original AnnData object\n    adata.obsm['X_emb'] = adata_corrected.obsm['X_pca']\n\n    return adata\n\n```\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: python storage/system/main.py\nLoading training dataset...\n  Data shape: (20000, 2000)\n  Batches: 4 batches\nFound eliminate_batch_effect_fn, executing...\n\n=== Running batch integration ===\n--- Running Contextual Combat ---\nWarning: Removing 2 batches with <2 cells\nWarning: NaN values detected in corrected data. Replacing with zeros.\n  Result shape: (20000, 2000)\n  Has embedding: True\n  Has graph: False\n\nResult saved to: storage/shared/tmp/4158b0fd-8317-4b5f-a496-c61369bfc389/result_human.h5ad\n\
    \nRESULT_UUID: 4158b0fd-8317-4b5f-a496-c61369bfc389\n\n\nSTDERR:\n/tmp/tmpq7a6_t09/submission.py:26: RuntimeWarning: invalid value encountered in divide\n  g_new = (t2 * n * g_hat + d_old * g_bar) / (t2 * n + d_old)\n\n```\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `storage write axiom/combat_centroid_alignment.py` (in Research Counter); YAML with fields: content\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- File created successfully: axiom/combat_centroid_alignment.py\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | Single-cell RNA-seq Batch Integration |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score | ARI | ASW_batch | ASW_label | Cell_cycle | Graph_conn | NMI | PCR | cLISI | iLISI | kBET |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n\
    | 1091 | 1 | Hybrid v4: Latent Standardization + MNN Residual Correction | Axiom I | 709 | 0.4697 | 0.411 | 0.538 | 0.216 | 0.368 | 0.830 | 0.629 | 0.000 | 0.990 | 0.000 | 0.716 |\n| 1089 | 1 | MNN-based Correction in Latent Space | Axiom I | 707 | 0.5728 | 0.757 | 0.450 | 0.224 | 0.366 | 0.860 | 0.702 | 0.277 | 0.993 | 0.277 | 0.823 |\n| 1087 | 1 | Hybrid v3: Latent Standardization + BBKNN Graph | Axiom I | 706 | 0.1759 | 0.117 | 0.000 | 0.000 | 0.000 | 0.210 | 0.431 | 0.000 | 1.000 | 0.000 | 0.000 |\n| 1085 | 1 | Latent Space Standardization (Mean and Variance Correction) | Axiom I | 705 | 0.6173 | 0.589 | 0.648 | 0.220 | 0.368 | 0.873 | 0.685 | 1.000 | 0.991 | 0.023 | 0.776 |\n| 1082 | 1 | Iterative Centroid Alignment in PCA Space | Axiom I | 703 | 0.5787 | 0.462 | 0.624 | 0.221 | 0.348 | 0.888 | 0.671 | 0.979 | 0.991 | 0.006 | 0.599 |\n| 1080 | 1 | Hybrid v2: PCA Centroid Alignment + BBKNN Graph | Axiom I | 702 | 0.1760 | 0.117 | 0.000 | 0.000 | 0.000 | 0.199 | 0.444 | 0.000 | 1.000\
    \ | 0.000 | 0.000 |\n| 1078 | 1 | Latent Space Correction via PCA Centroid Alignment | Axiom I | 701 | 0.5751 | 0.433 | 0.623 | 0.219 | 0.348 | 0.877 | 0.659 | 1.000 | 0.990 | 0.004 | 0.599 |\n| 1077 | 1 | Hybrid Method: Combat Correction followed by BBKNN Graph | Axiom I | 700 | 0.1858 | 0.155 | 0.000 | 0.000 | 0.000 | 0.241 | 0.439 | 0.000 | 1.000 | 0.023 | 0.000 |\n| 1071 | 1 | Replication of Combat Manual Baseline | Axiom I | 699 | 0.5894 | 0.493 | 0.664 | 0.223 | 0.323 | 0.885 | 0.683 | 1.000 | 0.988 | 0.033 | 0.602 |\n| 2 | 1 | Combat Manual Baseline | System | 0 | 0.5895 | 0.493 | 0.664 | 0.223 | 0.323 | 0.885 | 0.683 | 1.000 | 0.988 | 0.033 | 0.603 |\n\nPage 5 of 6 (sorted by: id)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-6, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer\
    \ to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help research}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
