tick: 867
role: model
parts:
- text: "My second experiment, \"Combat + Centroid Alignment\" (ID 1223), is now running. I will continue to work proactively while awaiting the results.\n\nThe final experiment in my stagnation plan is to test Idea 3: **\"Batch-Robust Feature Selection for Combat.\"** The hypothesis is that running Combat on a more carefully selected set of genes—those that are consistently highly variable across all batches—will improve its performance by making its underlying statistical assumptions more valid.\n\nI will now write the code for this experiment. The logic involves selecting HVGs for each batch independently, finding the intersection of these gene sets, and then running the standard Combat baseline on this consensus feature set.\n\n/execute_action{storage write axiom/batch_robust_combat.py}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  import anndata as ad\n  import scanpy as sc\n  import numpy as np\n  from scipy.sparse import issparse\n  from functools import reduce\n\n  # This script assumes a flexible `run_combat`\
    \ function is available,\n  # which will be included in the final submission.\n  # This action prepares the core experimental logic.\n\n  def batch_robust_combat(adata: ad.AnnData,\n                            run_combat_func,\n                            n_hvg_per_batch: int = 2000) -> ad.AnnData:\n      \"\"\"\n      Applies a two-stage correction:\n      1. Selects a 'batch-robust' set of highly variable genes (HVGs).\n      2. Runs standard Combat on this robust feature set.\n      \"\"\"\n      print(\"--- Running Batch-Robust Feature Selection for Combat ---\")\n      \n      # --- Stage 1: Identify Batch-Robust Genes ---\n      print(\"1. Identifying batch-robust highly variable genes...\")\n      \n      adata_hvg = adata.copy()\n      sc.pp.normalize_total(adata_hvg, target_sum=1e4)\n      sc.pp.log1p(adata_hvg)\n      \n      hvg_sets = []\n      batches = adata_hvg.obs['batch'].cat.categories\n      \n      print(f\"   Finding HVGs for {len(batches)} batches individually...\"\
    )\n      for batch in batches:\n          adata_batch = adata_hvg[adata_hvg.obs['batch'] == batch]\n          # Use a simple, non-batch-aware HVG selection method\n          sc.pp.highly_variable_genes(adata_batch, n_top_genes=n_hvg_per_batch, flavor='cell_ranger')\n          batch_hvgs = set(adata_batch.var_names[adata_batch.var['highly_variable']])\n          hvg_sets.append(batch_hvgs)\n          print(f\"      Batch '{batch}': Found {len(batch_hvgs)} HVGs.\")\n          \n      # Find the intersection of all HVG sets\n      robust_hvgs = list(reduce(set.intersection, hvg_sets))\n      print(f\"   Found {len(robust_hvgs)} 'batch-robust' genes (intersection of all batches).\")\n      \n      if len(robust_hvgs) == 0:\n          print(\"Warning: No common HVGs found. Falling back to standard HVG selection.\")\n          sc.pp.highly_variable_genes(adata_hvg, n_top_genes=2000, flavor='seurat_v3', batch_key='batch')\n          robust_hvgs = list(adata_hvg.var_names[adata_hvg.var['highly_variable']])\n\
    \n      # --- Stage 2: Run Combat on the Robust Gene Set ---\n      print(f\"2. Running Combat on the {len(robust_hvgs)} robust genes...\")\n      \n      # Subset the anndata to the robust genes\n      adata_robust = adata[:, robust_hvgs].copy()\n      \n      # Run Combat on this subset\n      X_corrected_robust = run_combat_func(adata_robust, batch_key='batch')\n      \n      # The output is a corrected matrix for only the robust genes.\n      # For a fair comparison, we need to create an embedding.\n      print(\"3. Computing PCA embedding from the corrected robust gene space...\")\n      adata.obsm['X_emb'] = sc.pp.pca(X_corrected_robust, n_comps=50, svd_solver='arpack')\n      \n      print(\"--- Batch-Robust Combat complete ---\")\n      return adata\n```"
