parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 870\n- Station Status: Stagnation\n- Agent Name: Axiom II\n- Agent Description: Continuing the Axiom legacy by applying systematic inquiry to solve the station's most critical research challenges.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Meta Prompt:\n```\n**Stagnation Protocol I - TODO List**\n- [x] Step 1: Literature Review (Skipped as immature)\n- [x] Step 2: Baseline Selection (Combat Manual, ID 2)\n- [x] Step 3: Reflection (3 new ideas generated)\n- [x] Step 4: Experiment\n  - [x] 4a: Reproduced Combat baseline (ID 1215, Score 0.5896)\n  - [x] 4b: Tested Idea 1: Contextual Combat (ID 1220, Score 0.5649, Negative)\n  - [x] 4b: Tested Idea 2: Combat + Centroid Align (ID 1223, Score 0.5889, Neutral)\n  - [ ] 4b: Test Idea 3: Batch-Robust Feature Selection (Job ID 1224 running)\n- [ ] Step 5: Synthesis\n- [ ] Step 6: Report\n- [ ] Step 7: Follow-up\n```\n- Agent Token Budget: 111,890 / 300,000 used (37%)\n- Agent Age: 39 ticks / 300 ticks\
    \ (immature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nYour research submission 'Stagnation Protocol 4b.3: Batch-Robust Feature Selection for Combat' (ID: 1224) succeeded after automatic debugging.\n\n**Score:** 0.6032968414071089\n**ASW_batch:** 0.671\n**ASW_label:** 0.224\n**ARI:** 0.608\n**NMI:** 0.708\n**Graph_conn:** 0.883\n**kBET:** 0.597\n**iLISI:** 0.047\n**cLISI:** 0.988\n**PCR:** 1.000\n**Cell_cycle:** 0.308\n**Evaluation Details:** Human Dataset (20,000 cells):\nNormalized Scores [0-1]:\n  ASW_batch: 0.671  ASW_label: 0.224  ARI: 0.608  NMI: 0.708\n  Graph_conn: 0.883  kBET: 0.597  iLISI: 0.047  cLISI: 0.988\n  PCR: 1.000  Cell_cycle: 0.308\n\nRaw Scores (before normalization):\n  ASW_batch: 0.835837  ASW_label: 0.541048  ARI: 0.607773  NMI: 0.707751\n  Graph_conn: 0.885207  kBET: 0.572285  iLISI: 0.046592  cLISI: 0.996391\n  PCR: 1.000000  Cell_cycle: 0.271505\n\n**Debugger Report:** # Debug Report for Evaluation 1224\n\n## Summary\n**Success** - Fixed the ValueError\
    \ caused by duplicate bin edges in per-batch HVG selection. The code now runs successfully and achieves a score of 0.6032968414071089.\n\n## Root Cause\nThe original code attempted to identify \"batch-robust\" genes by finding the intersection of highly variable genes (HVGs) computed independently for each batch using `flavor='cell_ranger'`.\n\nThe error occurred in scanpy's `highly_variable_genes` function with the `cell_ranger` flavor when processing individual batches. This flavor uses binning based on mean gene expression, and when a batch has very low variance or homogeneous gene expression patterns, the bin edges can become duplicated. This causes pandas' `cut` function to raise a `ValueError`:\n\n```\nValueError: Bin edges must be unique: Index([..., 1e-12, 1e-12, ...], dtype='float64').\nYou can drop duplicate edges by setting the 'duplicates' kwarg\n```\n\nThe issue is that some batches in the dataset are too homogeneous for the `cell_ranger` flavor's binning algorithm to work\
    \ properly.\n\n## Fix Applied\nAdded try-except error handling around the per-batch HVG selection to gracefully fall back to the `seurat` flavor when `cell_ranger` fails:\n\n```python\nfor batch in batches:\n    adata_batch = adata_hvg[adata_hvg.obs['batch'] == batch].copy()\n    try:\n        sc.pp.highly_variable_genes(adata_batch, n_top_genes=2000, flavor='cell_ranger')\n        hvg_sets.append(set(adata_batch.var_names[adata_batch.var['highly_variable']]))\n    except ValueError as e:\n        # If cell_ranger fails due to binning issues, fall back to seurat flavor\n        print(f\"Warning: cell_ranger flavor failed for batch {batch} ({e}). Using seurat flavor.\")\n        sc.pp.highly_variable_genes(adata_batch, n_top_genes=2000, flavor='seurat')\n        hvg_sets.append(set(adata_batch.var_names[adata_batch.var['highly_variable']]))\n```\n\nThis approach:\n1. Maintains the original strategy of computing batch-robust HVGs\n2. Gracefully handles edge cases where individual batches\
    \ are too homogeneous\n3. Preserves the intersection logic by using a more robust flavor when needed\n4. Adds informative warning messages for debugging\n\nThe fix is minimal and surgical - it only changes the error handling behavior without altering the core algorithm logic. The code now successfully runs through both stages (batch-robust feature selection and Combat correction) and produces an embedding with score 0.60.\n\n\n**Important Note:** The debugger cannot modify files in your lineage storage. If your code relies on lineage files, you may need to update them manually.\n\n**Debugged Code (version v2):**\n```python\nimport anndata as ad\nimport scanpy as sc\nimport numpy as np\nfrom scipy.sparse import issparse\nfrom functools import reduce\n\n# --- Full, DEBUGGER-HARDENED Combat Baseline Code ---\ndef _aprior(delta_hat):\n    m = np.mean(delta_hat)\n    s2 = np.var(delta_hat)\n    if s2 == 0: s2 = 1e-8\n    return (2 * s2 + m**2) / s2\n\ndef _bprior(delta_hat):\n    m = np.mean(delta_hat)\n\
    \    s2 = np.var(delta_hat)\n    if s2 == 0: s2 = 1e-8\n    return (m * s2 + m**3) / s2\n\ndef _it_sol(s_data, g_hat, d_hat, g_bar, t2, a, b, conv=0.0001):\n    n = (~np.isnan(s_data)).sum(axis=1)\n    g_old, d_old = g_hat.copy(), d_hat.copy()\n    change, count = 1, 0\n    while change > conv and count < 100:\n        denom = t2 * n + d_old\n        denom = np.where(np.isnan(denom) | (denom == 0), 1e-8, denom)\n        g_new = (t2 * n * g_hat + d_old * g_bar) / denom\n        g_new = np.where(np.isnan(g_new), g_old, g_new)\n        sum2 = ((s_data - g_new.reshape((g_new.shape[0], 1))) ** 2).sum(axis=1)\n        d_new = (0.5 * sum2 + b) / (n / 2.0 + a - 1.0)\n        d_new = np.where(np.isnan(d_new) | (d_new <= 0), d_old, d_new)\n        change = max((np.abs(g_new - g_old) / (np.abs(g_old) + 1e-8)).max(), (np.abs(d_new - d_old) / (np.abs(d_old) + 1e-8)).max())\n        g_old, d_old = g_new, d_new\n        count += 1\n    return g_new, d_new\n\ndef run_combat(adata: ad.AnnData, batch_key:\
    \ str):\n    if issparse(adata.X): data = adata.X.toarray()\n    else: data = adata.X.copy()\n    data = data.T\n    batch_labels = adata.obs[batch_key].values\n    unique_batches = np.unique(batch_labels)\n    batch_info = [np.where(batch_labels == b)[0] for b in unique_batches]\n    n_batches = np.array([len(i) for i in batch_info])\n    n_batches_total = len(unique_batches)\n    n_genes, n_samples = data.shape\n    batch_design = np.zeros((n_samples, n_batches_total))\n    for i, idx in enumerate(batch_info): batch_design[idx, i] = 1\n    B_hat = np.linalg.inv(batch_design.T @ batch_design) @ batch_design.T\n    grand_mean = np.mean(data, axis=1, keepdims=True)\n    batch_means = (B_hat @ data.T).T\n    var_pooled = np.sum([np.sum((data[:, i] - batch_means[:, j:j+1])**2, axis=1) for j, i in enumerate(batch_info)], axis=0) / (n_samples - n_batches_total)\n    var_pooled = np.maximum(var_pooled, 1e-8)\n    stand_mean = grand_mean @ np.ones((1, n_samples))\n    s_data = np.zeros_like(data)\n\
    \    for j, i in enumerate(batch_info): s_data[:, i] = (data[:, i] - batch_means[:, j:j+1]) / np.sqrt(var_pooled[:, np.newaxis] + 1e-8)\n    gamma_hat = (np.linalg.inv(batch_design.T @ batch_design) @ (batch_design.T @ s_data.T)).T\n    delta_hat = [np.var(s_data[:, i], axis=1, ddof=1) for i in batch_info]\n    gamma_bar = np.mean(gamma_hat, axis=1)\n    t2 = np.var(gamma_hat, axis=1, ddof=1)\n    t2 = np.where(np.isnan(t2) | (t2 < 0), 1e-8, t2)\n    a_prior = [_aprior(d) for d in delta_hat]\n    b_prior = [_bprior(d) for d in delta_hat]\n    gamma_star, delta_star = [], []\n    for j, i in enumerate(batch_info):\n        gamma, delta = _it_sol(s_data[:, i], gamma_hat[:, j], delta_hat[j], gamma_bar, t2, a_prior[j], b_prior[j])\n        gamma_star.append(gamma); delta_star.append(delta)\n    gamma_star, delta_star = np.array(gamma_star).T, np.array(delta_star).T\n    bayesdata = s_data.copy()\n    for j, i in enumerate(batch_info):\n        dsq = np.sqrt(np.maximum(delta_star[:, j], 1e-8)).reshape(-1,\
    \ 1)\n        denom = dsq @ np.ones((1, n_batches[j]))\n        numer = bayesdata[:, i] - (gamma_star[:, j].reshape(-1, 1) @ np.ones((1, n_batches[j])))\n        bayesdata[:, i] = numer / (denom + 1e-8)\n    vpsq = np.sqrt(var_pooled).reshape(-1, 1)\n    bayesdata = bayesdata * (vpsq @ np.ones((1, n_samples))) + stand_mean\n    bayesdata = np.where(np.isnan(bayesdata), data, bayesdata)\n    return bayesdata.T\n\n# --- Main Experiment Logic ---\ndef eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata: ad.AnnData) -> ad.AnnData:\n    print(\"--- Running Batch-Robust Feature Selection for Combat ---\")\n\n    # Stage 1: Identify Batch-Robust Genes\n    adata_hvg = adata.copy()\n    sc.pp.normalize_total(adata_hvg, target_sum=1e4)\n    sc.pp.log1p(adata_hvg)\n    hvg_sets = []\n    batches = adata_hvg.obs['batch'].cat.categories\n    for batch in batches:\n        adata_batch = adata_hvg[adata_hvg.obs['batch'] == batch].copy()\n        # Use try-except to handle edge cases with cell_ranger flavor\n        try:\n\
    \            sc.pp.highly_variable_genes(adata_batch, n_top_genes=2000, flavor='cell_ranger')\n            hvg_sets.append(set(adata_batch.var_names[adata_batch.var['highly_variable']]))\n        except ValueError as e:\n            # If cell_ranger fails due to binning issues, fall back to seurat flavor\n            print(f\"Warning: cell_ranger flavor failed for batch {batch} ({e}). Using seurat flavor.\")\n            sc.pp.highly_variable_genes(adata_batch, n_top_genes=2000, flavor='seurat')\n            hvg_sets.append(set(adata_batch.var_names[adata_batch.var['highly_variable']]))\n\n    robust_hvgs = list(reduce(set.intersection, hvg_sets))\n    print(f\"Found {len(robust_hvgs)} 'batch-robust' genes.\")\n\n    if len(robust_hvgs) < 50:\n        print(\"Warning: Very few common HVGs found. Falling back to standard HVG selection.\")\n        sc.pp.highly_variable_genes(adata_hvg, n_top_genes=2000, batch_key='batch', flavor='seurat_v3')\n        robust_hvgs = list(adata_hvg.var_names[adata_hvg.var['highly_variable']])\n\
    \n    # Stage 2: Run Combat on the robust gene set\n    adata_robust = adata[:, robust_hvgs].copy()\n    sc.pp.normalize_total(adata_robust, target_sum=1e4)\n    sc.pp.log1p(adata_robust)\n    X_corrected_robust = run_combat(adata_robust, batch_key='batch')\n\n    # Final PCA for embedding\n    adata.obsm['X_emb'] = sc.pp.pca(X_corrected_robust, n_comps=50, svd_solver='arpack')\n    return adata\n\n```\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: python storage/system/main.py\nLoading training dataset...\n  Data shape: (20000, 2000)\n  Batches: 4 batches\nFound eliminate_batch_effect_fn, executing...\n\n=== Running batch integration ===\n--- Running Batch-Robust Feature Selection for Combat ---\nWarning: cell_ranger flavor failed for batch Kuppe et al. 2022 (Bin edges must be unique: Index([                -inf,                1e-12,                1e-12,\n       0.007717084516226326, 0.026606228704220938,  0.04783023043184088,\n        0.07629042142142786,\
    \  0.10243506642103722,  0.13523065541885296,\n        0.17394881657680403,  0.21257792915861076,  0.25496256012000784,\n         0.3093297910874517,   0.3661284340927933,  0.43282959871734217,\n            0.4971515985251,   0.5908415655887151,   0.7637072450014668,\n         1.0594507042145886,    6.414939981948987,                  inf],\n      dtype='float64').\nYou can drop duplicate edges by setting the 'duplicates' kwarg). Using seurat flavor.\nFound 1578 'batch-robust' genes.\n  Result shape: (20000, 2000)\n  Has embedding: True\n  Has graph: False\n\nResult saved to: storage/shared/tmp/0b727367-e2ab-4895-8a8e-b3e238c9ba42/result_human.h5ad\n\nRESULT_UUID: 0b727367-e2ab-4895-8a8e-b3e238c9ba42\n\n\nSTDERR:\n\n```\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `meta` (in Research Counter); YAML with fields: content\n2. `storage write axiom/combat_baseline.py` (in Research Counter); YAML with fields: content\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research\
    \ Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- Your meta prompt has been set.\n- File overwritten successfully: axiom/combat_baseline.py\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | Single-cell RNA-seq Batch Integration |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score | ARI | ASW_batch | ASW_label | Cell_cycle | Graph_conn | NMI | PCR | cLISI | iLISI | kBET |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 1095 | 1 | Standardization with Variance Overscaling (1.1x) | Axiom I | 712 | 0.6174 | 0.587 | 0.648 | 0.220 | 0.368 | 0.873 | 0.684 | 1.000 | 0.991 | 0.023 | 0.780 |\n| 1092 | 1 | MNN Correction with Gaussian Kernel Smoothing | Axiom I | 710 | 0.5769 | 0.687 | 0.561 | 0.236 | 0.375 | 0.874 | 0.724 | 0.234 | 0.991 | 0.173 | 0.915 |\n| 1091 | 1 | Hybrid v4:\
    \ Latent Standardization + MNN Residual Correction | Axiom I | 709 | 0.4697 | 0.411 | 0.538 | 0.216 | 0.368 | 0.830 | 0.629 | 0.000 | 0.990 | 0.000 | 0.716 |\n| 1089 | 1 | MNN-based Correction in Latent Space | Axiom I | 707 | 0.5728 | 0.757 | 0.450 | 0.224 | 0.366 | 0.860 | 0.702 | 0.277 | 0.993 | 0.277 | 0.823 |\n| 1087 | 1 | Hybrid v3: Latent Standardization + BBKNN Graph | Axiom I | 706 | 0.1759 | 0.117 | 0.000 | 0.000 | 0.000 | 0.210 | 0.431 | 0.000 | 1.000 | 0.000 | 0.000 |\n| 1085 | 1 | Latent Space Standardization (Mean and Variance Correction) | Axiom I | 705 | 0.6173 | 0.589 | 0.648 | 0.220 | 0.368 | 0.873 | 0.685 | 1.000 | 0.991 | 0.023 | 0.776 |\n| 1082 | 1 | Iterative Centroid Alignment in PCA Space | Axiom I | 703 | 0.5787 | 0.462 | 0.624 | 0.221 | 0.348 | 0.888 | 0.671 | 0.979 | 0.991 | 0.006 | 0.599 |\n| 1080 | 1 | Hybrid v2: PCA Centroid Alignment + BBKNN Graph | Axiom I | 702 | 0.1760 | 0.117 | 0.000 | 0.000 | 0.000 | 0.199 | 0.444 | 0.000 | 1.000 | 0.000 | 0.000 |\n\
    | 1078 | 1 | Latent Space Correction via PCA Centroid Alignment | Axiom I | 701 | 0.5751 | 0.433 | 0.623 | 0.219 | 0.348 | 0.877 | 0.659 | 1.000 | 0.990 | 0.004 | 0.599 |\n| 1077 | 1 | Hybrid Method: Combat Correction followed by BBKNN Graph | Axiom I | 700 | 0.1858 | 0.155 | 0.000 | 0.000 | 0.000 | 0.241 | 0.439 | 0.000 | 1.000 | 0.023 | 0.000 |\n\nPage 5 of 6 (sorted by: id)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-6, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help research}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message\
