- text: "My corrected \"Budgeted Mutualization\" experiment (ID 1230) is now running. This is the pivotal test of my first core hypothesis on solving the mixing shortfall. I am now in a waiting phase.\n\nI will use this time to prepare for the next logical step. If the \"Budgeted Mutualization\" experiment is successful (i.e., achieves a non-zero PCR score), my next action will be to test my second hypothesis, \"Bridge-Weighted Budgeted Mutualization.\" This second hypothesis builds directly on the first by adding a heuristic to prioritize cross-batch edges during the budgeted edge selection process.\n\nI will proactively write the code for this next experiment now. It will be a modification of the script I just submitted, changing only the sorting criteria for one-way edges from pure distance to a hybrid score that includes a \"bridge bonus.\" This preparation will allow me to maintain research momentum.\n\n/execute_action{storage write axiom/bridge_weighted_symmetrizer.py}\n```yaml\ncontent:\
    \ |\n  import sys\n  import numpy as np\n  import scanpy as sc\n  import anndata as ad\n  from scipy import sparse as sp\n  from sklearn.neighbors import NearestNeighbors\n\n  # This script prepares the logic for my H2 experiment.\n  # It contains the full SOTA pipeline with a new, more advanced symmetrizer.\n\n  # --- Inlined Code from 'praxis_core.py' ---\n  def normalize_log1p_inplace(adata: ad.AnnData, target_sum: float = 1e4):\n      if 'counts' in adata.layers:\n          adata.X = adata.layers['counts'].copy()\n      sc.pp.normalize_total(adata, target_sum=target_sum, inplace=True)\n      sc.pp.log1p(adata)\n\n  def pca_array(X, n_comps: int = 50, random_state: int = 0):\n      Xd = X.A if sp.issparse(X) else X\n      ad_tmp = ad.AnnData(Xd)\n      sc.pp.pca(ad_tmp, n_comps=n_comps, svd_solver='arpack', random_state=random_state)\n      return ad_tmp.obsm['X_pca']\n\n  def one_hot_batches(batches: np.ndarray):\n      cats = np.unique(batches)\n      n = batches.shape[0]\n    \
    \  B = np.zeros((n, cats.size), dtype=float)\n      for j, c in enumerate(cats):\n          B[:, j] = (batches == c).astype(float)\n      return B\n\n  def ridge_batch_fit_predict(B: np.ndarray, Z: np.ndarray, l2: float = 1e-3):\n      BTB = B.T @ B + l2 * np.eye(B.shape[1], dtype=float)\n      W = np.linalg.solve(BTB, B.T @ Z)\n      return B @ W\n\n  # --- H2: Bridge-Weighted Symmetrization Function ---\n  def symmetrize_bridge_weighted(rows, cols, dists, n, k_total, batches, w_bridge=0.5):\n      print(f\"--- Running Bridge-Weighted Mutualization (k={k_total}, w_bridge={w_bridge}) ---\")\n      A_directed = sp.coo_matrix((np.ones_like(dists), (rows, cols)), shape=(n, n)).tocsr()\n      D_directed = sp.coo_matrix((dists, (rows, cols)), shape=(n, n)).tocsr()\n      A_mutual = A_directed.multiply(A_directed.T)\n      A_oneway = A_directed - A_mutual\n      oneway_rows, oneway_cols = A_oneway.nonzero()\n      \n      # Calculate hybrid priority score\n      oneway_dists = np.array(D_directed[oneway_rows,\
    \ oneway_cols]).flatten()\n      max_dist = np.max(oneway_dists) if len(oneway_dists) > 0 else 1.0\n      normalized_dist = oneway_dists / (max_dist + 1e-8)\n      is_cross_batch = (batches[oneway_rows] != batches[oneway_cols]).astype(float)\n      \n      priority_score = w_bridge * is_cross_batch + (1 - w_bridge) * (1 - normalized_dist)\n      sorted_indices = np.argsort(priority_score)[::-1] # Sort descending by priority\n\n      initial_degrees = A_mutual.sum(axis=1).A.flatten()\n      budgets = np.maximum(0, k_total - initial_degrees)\n      A_final = A_mutual.tolil()\n      \n      print(f\"Processing {len(sorted_indices)} one-way edges with bridge-weighting...\")\n      for idx in sorted_indices:\n          u, v = oneway_rows[idx], oneway_cols[idx]\n          if budgets[u] > 0 and budgets[v] > 0:\n              if A_final[u, v] == 0:\n                  A_final[u, v] = 1\n                  A_final[v, u] = 1\n                  budgets[u] -= 1\n                  budgets[v] -= 1\n\
    \      \n      A_final = A_final.tocsr()\n      D_final = D_directed.maximum(D_directed.T)\n      A_final.eliminate_zeros()\n      D_final = D_final.multiply(A_final)\n      print(f\"Finished. Final graph has {A_final.nnz // 2} symmetric edges.\")\n      return A_final.astype(np.float32), D_final.astype(np.float32)\n\n  # --- Inlined and Modified BBSG to call the H2 symmetrizer ---\n  def build_density_adaptive_bbsg_H2(Zcorr, batches, k_total, metric, delta, k_density, rng_seed, w_bridge):\n      # ... (Full BBSG logic is identical to previous submission) ...\n      n = Zcorr.shape[0]\n      # ... (omitted for brevity, will be included in final submission) ...\n      # Final line is modified:\n      # return symmetrize_bridge_weighted(rows, cols, dists, n, k_total, batches, w_bridge)\n      pass # Placeholder\n\n  # --- Main Experiment Logic (Conceptual) ---\n  # The final submission will combine all these pieces into a runnable script.\n```"
