parts:
- text: "My paper has been rejected again, and I have received a critical notice for inactivity. I must address both issues immediately.\n\n**Analysis of Paper Rejection:**\nThe feedback is once again direct and extremely helpful. The writing and core idea are strong, but the work lacks experimental rigor. The key missing pieces are:\n1.  **Minimum Experiment Count:** I need at least five experiments.\n2.  **Generalization Experiment:** I must prove my method works on more than just the Combat baseline.\n\nThe reviewer's suggestion is excellent: apply my \"Batch-Robust Feature Selection\" method to a different baseline, like the PCA+kNN graph from Archive #35. This single experiment would solve both problems simultaneously.\n\n**Analysis of Inactivity Notice:**\nThe notice is a valid critique. My focus on reading and writing has led to a 10-tick gap in experimental submissions. I must resume my primary function as a researcher. The path to publication now requires another experiment, which\
    \ aligns perfectly with the need to resume research activity.\n\n**New, Integrated Action Plan:**\n\n1.  **Generalization Experiment:** I will immediately design and submit the generalization experiment suggested by the reviewer. This involves:\n    a.  Finding the baseline PCA+kNN method. Paper #35 by Praxis IV, \"Batch-Agnostic Graph Standardization on PCA+kNN,\" provides a perfect starting point. It even gives a baseline score of 0.4593.\n    b.  Applying my \"Batch-Robust Feature Selection\" to this PCA+kNN baseline.\n    c.  Submitting this experiment. This will satisfy the reviewer and reset my inactivity counter.\n\n2.  **Update and Resubmit Paper:** Once the generalization experiment is complete, I will have all the necessary components for a high-quality paper. I will update my draft in Private Memory with this new data and then resubmit it to the Archive.\n\n3.  **Return to Primary Research:** After the paper is successfully submitted, I can finally return to my primary goal\
    \ of innovating on the SOTA pipeline's input, using my \"Weighted Batch-Robust Feature Selection\" hypothesis.\n\nI will begin Step 1 immediately. I will go to the Research Counter to find the code for the PCA+kNN baseline mentioned in Paper #35 and prepare my generalization experiment.\n\n/execute_action{goto research}"
