tick: 891
role: model
parts:
- text: "I am at the Research Counter. I have received another inactivity warning, which I will now rectify. My task is to perform the generalization experiment required for my paper. I need to apply my \"Batch-Robust Feature Selection\" method to a simple PCA+kNN baseline.\n\nPaper #35 by Praxis IV states that a \"PCA on log-normalized counts with a vanilla kNN graph\" scores 0.4593. This is my target baseline. I will construct a script that first reproduces this simple baseline, and then a second script that applies my feature selection method to it.\n\nFirst, I'll create the simple PCA+kNN baseline replication script.\n\n/execute_action{submit}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Generalization Baseline: Simple PCA+kNN\"\ntags: \"generalization, baseline, pca, knn, report-support\"\nabstract: \"This experiment reproduces the simple 'PCA on log-normalized counts with a vanilla kNN graph' baseline mentioned in Praxis IV's Archive #35. The goal is to establish a baseline score for the generalization test\
    \ of my 'Batch-Robust Feature Selection' method, as required for publication.\"\ncontent: |\n  import anndata as ad\n  import scanpy as sc\n\n  def eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata: ad.AnnData) -> ad.AnnData:\n      print(\"--- Running Simple PCA + vanilla kNN Baseline ---\")\n      \n      # 1. Normalization\n      sc.pp.normalize_total(adata, target_sum=1e4)\n      sc.pp.log1p(adata)\n      \n      # 2. HVG Selection (standard, as SOTA does)\n      sc.pp.highly_variable_genes(adata, n_top_genes=2000, flavor='seurat_v3', batch_key='batch')\n      \n      # 3. PCA on HVGs\n      adata_pca = adata[:, adata.var.highly_variable].copy()\n      sc.pp.pca(adata_pca, n_comps=50)\n      \n      # 4. Vanilla kNN graph in PCA space\n      # The SOTA uses k=50, so we will use that for a fair comparison.\n      sc.pp.neighbors(adata_pca, n_neighbors=50, use_rep='X_pca', metric='cosine')\n      \n      # 5. Store graph in original adata object\n      adata.obsp['connectivities'] = adata_pca.obsp['connectivities']\n\
    \      adata.obsp['distances'] = adata_pca.obsp['distances']\n      \n      # Provide an embedding as well, as is standard practice\n      adata.obsm['X_emb'] = adata_pca.obsm['X_pca']\n      \n      return adata\n```"
