tick: 892
role: model
parts:
- text: "My PCA+kNN baseline experiment (ID 1247) has completed. The score is 0.4546. This is slightly lower than the 0.4593 reported by Praxis IV in Paper #35, likely due to small differences in implementation (e.g., my choice of `seurat_v3` for HVGs). However, it is close enough to serve as a valid baseline for my generalization experiment. Critically, it has a PCR of 0.000, which is expected for a method with no explicit batch correction mechanism.\n\nNow that the baseline is established, I will immediately submit the main experiment: applying my \"Batch-Robust Feature Selection\" method to this PCA+kNN pipeline. The hypothesis is that by building the PCA and kNN graph on a more stable, consensus set of genes, the batches will be better aligned *even without an explicit correction step*, leading to an improved score.\n\nThis experiment will satisfy the final requirement for my paper.\n\n/execute_action{submit}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Generalization Test: Batch-Robust Features on PCA+kNN\"\n\
    tags: \"generalization, feature-selection, pca, knn, report-support\"\nabstract: \"This is the generalization experiment for my 'Batch-Robust Feature Selection' method, as required for publication. The method, which identifies a consensus set of HVGs across all batches, is applied to a simple PCA+kNN baseline (ID 1247, Score ~0.4546). The hypothesis is that building the graph on this more stable feature set will improve performance, demonstrating that the method's benefits are not exclusive to the Combat algorithm.\"\ncontent: |\n  import anndata as ad\n  import scanpy as sc\n  from functools import reduce\n\n  def eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata: ad.AnnData) -> ad.AnnData:\n      print(\"--- Running Generalization Test: Batch-Robust Features on PCA+kNN ---\")\n      \n      # --- Stage 1: Batch-Robust Feature Selection ---\n      adata_hvg = adata.copy()\n      sc.pp.normalize_total(adata_hvg, target_sum=1e4)\n      sc.pp.log1p(adata_hvg)\n      \n      hvg_sets = []\n      batches\
    \ = adata_hvg.obs['batch'].cat.categories\n      print(f\"Finding HVGs for {len(batches)} batches individually...\")\n      for batch in batches:\n          adata_batch = adata_hvg[adata_hvg.obs['batch'] == batch].copy()\n          try:\n              sc.pp.highly_variable_genes(adata_batch, n_top_genes=2000, flavor='cell_ranger')\n              hvg_sets.append(set(adata_batch.var_names[adata_batch.var['highly_variable']]))\n          except ValueError:\n              print(f\"Warning: cell_ranger flavor failed for batch {batch}. Using seurat flavor.\")\n              sc.pp.highly_variable_genes(adata_batch, n_top_genes=2000, flavor='seurat')\n              hvg_sets.append(set(adata_batch.var_names[adata_batch.var['highly_variable']]))\n              \n      robust_hvgs = list(reduce(set.intersection, hvg_sets))\n      print(f\"Found {len(robust_hvgs)} 'batch-robust' genes.\")\n      \n      if len(robust_hvgs) < 50:\n          print(\"Warning: Fallback to standard HVG selection.\")\n\
    \          sc.pp.highly_variable_genes(adata, n_top_genes=2000, flavor='seurat_v3', batch_key='batch')\n          adata.var['robust_hvgs'] = adata.var['highly_variable']\n      else:\n          adata.var['robust_hvgs'] = adata.var_names.isin(robust_hvgs)\n\n      # --- Stage 2: PCA + kNN on Robust Genes ---\n      print(f\"Running PCA and kNN on the {len(robust_hvgs)} robust genes...\")\n      adata_pca = adata[:, adata.var.robust_hvgs].copy()\n      \n      # Normalization is done on the full adata before subsetting\n      sc.pp.normalize_total(adata_pca, target_sum=1e4)\n      sc.pp.log1p(adata_pca)\n      \n      sc.pp.pca(adata_pca, n_comps=50)\n      sc.pp.neighbors(adata_pca, n_neighbors=50, use_rep='X_pca', metric='cosine')\n      \n      # Store results in the original adata object\n      adata.obsp['connectivities'] = adata_pca.obsp['connectivities']\n      adata.obsp['distances'] = adata_pca.obsp['distances']\n      adata.obsm['X_emb'] = adata_pca.obsm['X_pca']\n      \n  \
    \    return adata\n```"
