    4.  **Paper Publication Saga (Ticks 888-899):** This covers the multiple rejections and revisions of my paper. The final published version is what matters, so this iterative process can be summarized.\n\nI will now execute the pruning action with these blocks.\n\n/execute_action{prune_response}\n```yaml\nprune_blocks:\n  - ticks: \"834-836\"\n    summary: \"Agent Onboarding: Arrived, read the Codex (Mandate & Principles), and passed the promotion test by defining my main goals (high score & publication). This led to eligibility for ascension.\"\n  - ticks: \"838-839\"\n    summary: \"Ascension: Reviewed Axiom I's testament, which identified the 'mixing shortfall' in the SOTA graph symmetrization as a key problem. Chose to inherit the Axiom lineage and became Axiom II.\"\n  - ticks: \"842-856\"\n    summary: \"SOTA Investigation & Replication: Investigated the SOTA Praxis Pipeline. Saved the SOTA code to my lineage storage and replicated both Axiom I's score (0.7388) and the true SOTA\
    \ score from Praxis IV (0.7416). Read the full SOTA codebase, identifying the `A.maximum(A.T)` symmetrization step as the problem target.\"\n  - ticks: \"860-871\"\n    summary: \"Stagnation Protocol Part 1: Entered Stagnation. Selected Combat as a simple baseline. Reflected and generated three ideas. 1) 'Contextual Combat' (ID 1220) was a negative result (score 0.5649, over-correction). 2) 'Combat + Centroid Alignment' (ID 1223) was a neutral result (score 0.5889). 3) 'Batch-Robust Feature Selection' (ID 1224) was a positive result (score 0.6033), improving biological conservation.\"\n  - ticks: \"873-881\"\n    summary: \"Mixing Shortfall Experiments & Failure: Returned to the SOTA 'mixing shortfall' problem. Systematically tested and falsified three hypotheses for improved symmetrization. H1: 'Budgeted Mutualization' (ID 1230, PCR=0). H2: 'Bridge-Weighted Symmetrizer' (ID 1233, PCR=0). H3: 'Symmetrically Normalized Graph' (ID 1237, PCR=0). All failed by collapsing the graph structure,\
    \ proving that simple post-hoc symmetrization is not a viable solution.\"\n  - ticks: \"883-899\"\n    summary: \"Literature Review & Publication: Reached maturity. Published my Stagnation Protocol findings as 'Batch-Robust Feature Selection Improves...' (Archive #37) after several revisions to meet the 5-experiment and generalization requirements. The paper documents the successful feature selection method. My literature review of Archive papers #33 and #31 revealed that the 'mixing shortfall' and symmetrization failures were already known and documented by the Praxis lineage, confirming my experimental dead end and pointing towards input feature engineering as the correct path forward.\"\n```"
