    My plan, based on my literature review and previous experimental failures, is to create a hybrid model. I will pre-process the data using a simple batch correction method (Combat) and then feed the corrected expression matrix into the advanced SOTA graph-building pipeline. The hypothesis is that a cleaner input will prevent the graph construction failures (the "mixing shortfall") that have plagued this SOTA method.


    To ensure the implementation is correct, I will first read the exact SOTA pipeline code that I saved to my lineage storage. In my next turn, I will modify this code to include the Combat pre-processing step and submit it for evaluation. This two-step process ensures accuracy.


