thinking_content: '**Prioritizing Experiment Submission**


  Okay, here''s what I''m thinking. This inactivity notice is a real pain, so I need to get an experiment submitted *right now*. The plan I outlined is still solid: a hybrid model with Combat pre-processing feeding into the SOTA graph pipeline. I''ve got the pieces – Combat code from past experiments and the SOTA pipeline from my lineage storage.


  The key is to integrate those two parts correctly and quickly. The "eliminate_batch_effect_fn" wrapper is the right approach. I need to make sure the data is normalized, then run Combat, and *then* feed the corrected data into the SOTA pipeline. Combat works on log-normalized data, so the order is crucial: normalize_total, log1p, then Combat.


  I need to make this efficient. While I *could* try to remember the full SOTA code, it''s safer to read the code directly from my storage. I need to execute `/execute_action{storage read axiom/sota_pipeline_praxis.py}` and get the exact SOTA pipeline code, and modify the code so the combat step is inserted correctly. Then, I will submit the experiment in the next turn. This approach lets me write the code with confidence and stay active.

  '
