tick: 910
role: model
parts:
- text: "I have successfully saved my feature engineering utility functions to my lineage storage. Now I will test my new, more advanced feature selection method: \"Union HVGs with Batch Correlation Filter.\"\n\nThe hypothesis is that this method will be superior to the simple intersection method used by Daedalus IV because it considers a wider pool of potentially important genes (the union) and then uses a more principled approach (correlation with batch labels) to filter out confounding variables. This should provide the SOTA pipeline with a richer, cleaner feature set, potentially pushing the score beyond what has been seen so far.\n\nI will now submit this experiment.\n\n/execute_action{submit}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Advanced Feature Selection: Union HVG + Batch Correlation Filter on SOTA Pipeline\"\ntags: \"feature-engineering, hvg, batch-correlation, sota, graph\"\nabstract: \"Building upon the success of applying 'Batch-Robust Feature Selection' to the SOTA pipeline (Daedalus IV, ID 1261),\
    \ this experiment introduces a more advanced feature selection method. Instead of a simple intersection of HVGs, we take the union of HVGs across all batches to capture a wider range of biological signals. We then apply a novel filtering step, removing genes that show high correlation with batch identity. This aims to provide the SOTA pipeline with a feature set that is both comprehensive and clean of batch-confounding signals, with the goal of surpassing the current SOTA score.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  import anndata as ad\n  import scanpy as sc\n  \n  # Import my new feature engineering functions\n  sys.path.append('storage/axiom')\n  from feature_engineering import get_union_features_batch_filtered\n  \n  # Import the SOTA pipeline function from Praxis lineage storage\n  sys.path.append('storage/praxis')\n  from best_mpb_daqb_kd22_k50 import eliminate_batch_effect_fn as run_sota_pipeline\n  \n  def eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata: ad.AnnData) -> ad.AnnData:\n      \"\"\"\n \
    \     Applies advanced feature selection and then runs the SOTA pipeline.\n      \"\"\"\n      print(\"--- Running Advanced Feature Selection + SOTA Graph ---\")\n      \n      # Step 1: Select features using the new method\n      # Using default n_top_genes=2000, corr_threshold=0.1\n      robust_genes = get_union_features_batch_filtered(adata.copy())\n      \n      # Step 2: Create a new AnnData object with only the selected features\n      adata_filtered = adata[:, robust_genes].copy()\n      \n      # Step 3: Run the SOTA pipeline on the filtered data\n      print(f\"Running SOTA graph pipeline on {len(robust_genes)} selected features...\")\n      adata_result = run_sota_pipeline(adata_filtered)\n      \n      # The SOTA pipeline returns an object with the reduced gene set.\n      # We need to return an object with the original 2000 genes for evaluation.\n      # Create a new adata object and copy the embedding and graph results.\n      final_adata = adata.copy()\n      final_adata.obsm['X_emb']\
    \ = adata_result.obsm['X_emb']\n      final_adata.obsp['connectivities'] = adata_result.obsp['connectivities']\n      final_adata.obsp['distances'] = adata_result.obsp['distances']\n      \n      return final_adata\n\n```"
