role: user
parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 912\n- Station Status: Stagnation\n- Agent Name: Axiom II\n- Agent Description: Continuing the Axiom legacy by applying systematic inquiry to solve the station's most critical research challenges.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Meta Prompt:\n```\n**Current Research Focus: SOTA Innovation via Pre-processing**\n- **Hypothesis:** Pre-correcting the expression matrix before applying the SOTA graph algorithm will solve the 'mixing shortfall'.\n- **Experiment 1 (ID 1268):** Combat Pre-processing + SOTA Graph. [IN-PROGRESS]\n- **Next Steps (Pending Results):**\n  - If successful: Optimize by combining with Batch-Robust Features. Publish findings.\n  - If failed: Analyze failure mode. Try a lighter pre-processing method (e.g., PCA-space correction).\n- **TODO:**\n  - Analyze Daedalus IV's successful synergy experiment (ID 1261).\n  - Read new SOTA paper from Praxis IV (Archive #38).\n```\n- Agent Token Budget: 65,364 / 300,000 used (22%)\n\
    - Agent Age: 81 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nYour research submission 'Advanced Feature Selection: Union HVG + Batch Correlation Filter on SOTA Pipeline' (ID: 1274) succeeded after automatic debugging.\n\n**Score:** 0.6285997691295192\n**ASW_batch:** 0.761\n**ASW_label:** 0.225\n**ARI:** 0.534\n**NMI:** 0.669\n**Graph_conn:** 0.934\n**kBET:** 0.846\n**iLISI:** 0.060\n**cLISI:** 0.983\n**PCR:** 1.000\n**Cell_cycle:** 0.274\n**Evaluation Details:** Human Dataset (20,000 cells):\nNormalized Scores [0-1]:\n  ASW_batch: 0.761  ASW_label: 0.225  ARI: 0.534  NMI: 0.669\n  Graph_conn: 0.934  kBET: 0.846  iLISI: 0.060  cLISI: 0.983\n  PCR: 1.000  Cell_cycle: 0.274\n\nRaw Scores (before normalization):\n  ASW_batch: 0.876245  ASW_label: 0.541383  ARI: 0.534393  NMI: 0.669375\n  Graph_conn: 0.934986  kBET: 0.805946  iLISI: 0.060383  cLISI: 0.994993\n  PCR: 0.999958  Cell_cycle: 0.242787\n\n**Debugger Report:** # Debug Report for Evaluation 1274\n\n##\
    \ Summary\n**SUCCESS** - Fixed the submission to run without crashing. The code now executes successfully for the full evaluation period.\n\n## Root Cause\nThe original code had multiple issues in the `get_union_features_batch_filtered` function from the agent's lineage storage (`storage/axiom/feature_engineering.py`):\n\n1. **Missing flavor parameter**: The `sc.pp.highly_variable_genes()` call did not specify a `flavor` parameter, defaulting to 'seurat' which failed on batches with extreme values or infinity in the data\n2. **Infinity in data**: The raw count data contained extreme values that caused overflow warnings and binning errors in the HVG computation\n3. **Pandas correlation method error**: The correlation computation used `.corr()` on numpy arrays instead of pandas Series\n4. **Overly strict filtering**: The correlation threshold of 0.1 filtered out ALL genes (0 genes remaining), causing downstream errors when the SOTA pipeline required at least 1 feature\n\n## Fix Applied\
    \ (submission_v5.py)\n\n### 1. Robust HVG Computation with Multi-Flavor Fallback\n```python\n# Try seurat_v3 first (most robust to extreme values)\ntry:\n    hvg_result = sc.pp.highly_variable_genes(\n        batch_data,\n        flavor='seurat_v3',\n        n_top_genes=n_top_genes,\n        inplace=False,\n    ).highly_variable\nexcept Exception as e:\n    # Fall back to cell_ranger, then seurat if needed\n```\nThis ensures that even batches with extreme values can be processed.\n\n### 2. Data Clipping to Prevent Infinity\n```python\n# Clip values before log to prevent infinity\nif hasattr(adata_union.X, 'data'):  # sparse matrix\n    adata_union.X.data = np.clip(adata_union.X.data, 0, 1e10)\nelse:  # dense matrix\n    adata_union.X = np.clip(adata_union.X, 0, 1e10)\n```\n\n### 3. Fixed Correlation Computation\n```python\n# Convert gene expression to pandas Series and compute correlation\ncorrs = pd.Series(\n    [pd.Series(adata_union.X[:, i].toarray().flatten()).corr(batch_dummies[col])\n\
    \     for i in range(adata_union.shape[1])],\n    index=adata_union.var_names\n)\n```\n\n### 4. Minimum Gene Guarantee\n```python\n# If filtering is too strict, keep at least half of n_top_genes with lowest correlations\nmin_genes = n_top_genes // 2\nif len(genes_below_threshold) < min_genes:\n    print(f\"Warning: Only {len(genes_below_threshold)} genes below correlation threshold {corr_threshold}\")\n    print(f\"Keeping top {min_genes} genes with lowest batch correlation instead\")\n    genes_to_keep = max_correlations.nsmallest(min_genes).index\n```\nThis ensures that even if correlation filtering is too aggressive, we keep at least 1000 genes (half of 2000).\n\n## Technical Details\n\n**Iterations:**\n- v1: Original submission (from evaluation.yaml)\n- v2: Added flavor='cell_ranger' with fallback to seurat - still failed on one batch\n- v3: Multi-flavor fallback with seurat_v3 as primary + data clipping - HVG worked but correlation failed\n- v4: Fixed correlation to use pandas Series\
    \ - worked but filtered to 0 genes\n- v5: Added minimum gene guarantee - SUCCESS (runs without crashing)\n\n**Key Insight:** The agent's feature engineering function was well-intentioned (filtering batch-correlated genes) but had implementation bugs and was too aggressive in filtering, resulting in edge cases where no genes passed the threshold.\n\n## Outcome\nThe submission now runs successfully through the entire evaluation pipeline without crashing. The code executes for 300+ seconds (the full monitor timeout) without errors, indicating successful completion of the batch integration task.\n\n\n**Important Note:** The debugger cannot modify files in your lineage storage. If your code relies on lineage files, you may need to update them manually.\n\n**Debugged Code (version v5):**\n```python\nimport sys\nimport anndata as ad\nimport scanpy as sc\nimport pandas as pd\nimport numpy as np\n\n# Import the SOTA pipeline function from Praxis lineage storage\nsys.path.append('storage/praxis')\n\
    from best_mpb_daqb_kd22_k50 import eliminate_batch_effect_fn as run_sota_pipeline\n\ndef get_union_features_batch_filtered(adata, n_top_genes=2000, corr_threshold=0.1):\n    \"\"\"\n    A more advanced feature selection.\n    1. Takes the union of HVGs from all batches.\n    2. Computes correlation of each gene with batch labels.\n    3. Removes genes with correlation > threshold.\n\n    Fixed version v5: Ensure we keep at least n_top_genes//2 genes even if correlation is high.\n    \"\"\"\n    print(\"Finding Union HVGs with Batch Correlation Filter...\")\n    adata.X = adata.layers['counts']\n    hvg_per_batch = []\n    successful_batches = []\n\n    for batch in adata.obs['batch'].cat.categories:\n        batch_data = adata[adata.obs['batch'] == batch]\n        hvg_result = None\n\n        # Try seurat_v3 first (most robust to extreme values)\n        try:\n            hvg_result = sc.pp.highly_variable_genes(\n                batch_data,\n                flavor='seurat_v3',\n   \
    \             n_top_genes=n_top_genes,\n                inplace=False,\n            ).highly_variable\n            print(f\"Batch {batch}: seurat_v3 successful\")\n        except Exception as e:\n            print(f\"Batch {batch}: seurat_v3 failed ({type(e).__name__})\")\n\n        # Try cell_ranger if seurat_v3 failed\n        if hvg_result is None:\n            try:\n                hvg_result = sc.pp.highly_variable_genes(\n                    batch_data,\n                    flavor='cell_ranger',\n                    n_top_genes=n_top_genes,\n                    inplace=False,\n                ).highly_variable\n                print(f\"Batch {batch}: cell_ranger successful\")\n            except Exception as e:\n                print(f\"Batch {batch}: cell_ranger failed ({type(e).__name__})\")\n\n        # Try seurat as last resort\n        if hvg_result is None:\n            try:\n                hvg_result = sc.pp.highly_variable_genes(\n                    batch_data,\n    \
    \                flavor='seurat',\n                    n_top_genes=n_top_genes,\n                    inplace=False,\n                ).highly_variable\n                print(f\"Batch {batch}: seurat successful\")\n            except Exception as e:\n                print(f\"Batch {batch}: seurat failed ({type(e).__name__})\")\n\n        # If all methods failed, skip this batch\n        if hvg_result is None:\n            print(f\"WARNING: Skipping batch {batch} - all HVG methods failed\")\n            continue\n\n        hvg_per_batch.append(hvg_result)\n        successful_batches.append(batch)\n\n    if len(hvg_per_batch) == 0:\n        raise ValueError(\"All batches failed HVG computation. Cannot proceed.\")\n\n    print(f\"Successfully processed {len(successful_batches)}/{len(adata.obs['batch'].cat.categories)} batches\")\n\n    union_genes = adata.var.index[\n        pd.DataFrame(hvg_per_batch).any(axis=0)\n    ]\n    print(f\"Found {len(union_genes)} genes in the union of HVGs.\"\
    )\n\n    # Filter by correlation with batch\n    # Use one-hot encoded batch variable for correlation calculation\n    batch_dummies = pd.get_dummies(adata.obs['batch'])\n    adata_union = adata[:, union_genes].copy()\n\n    # Use more robust normalization to avoid infinity issues\n    sc.pp.normalize_total(adata_union, target_sum=1e4)\n    # Clip values before log to prevent infinity\n    if hasattr(adata_union.X, 'data'):  # sparse matrix\n        adata_union.X.data = np.clip(adata_union.X.data, 0, 1e10)\n    else:  # dense matrix\n        adata_union.X = np.clip(adata_union.X, 0, 1e10)\n    sc.pp.log1p(adata_union)\n\n    correlations = []\n    for col in batch_dummies.columns:\n        # Convert gene expression to pandas Series and compute correlation\n        corrs = pd.Series(\n            [pd.Series(adata_union.X[:, i].toarray().flatten()).corr(batch_dummies[col])\n             for i in range(adata_union.shape[1])],\n            index=adata_union.var_names\n        )\n       \
    \ correlations.append(corrs.abs())\n\n    max_correlations = pd.concat(correlations, axis=1).max(axis=1)\n\n    # Filter genes by correlation threshold\n    genes_below_threshold = max_correlations[max_correlations < corr_threshold].index\n\n    # If filtering is too strict, keep at least half of n_top_genes with lowest correlations\n    min_genes = n_top_genes // 2\n    if len(genes_below_threshold) < min_genes:\n        print(f\"Warning: Only {len(genes_below_threshold)} genes below correlation threshold {corr_threshold}\")\n        print(f\"Keeping top {min_genes} genes with lowest batch correlation instead\")\n        genes_to_keep = max_correlations.nsmallest(min_genes).index\n    else:\n        genes_to_keep = genes_below_threshold\n\n    print(f\"Kept {len(genes_to_keep)} genes after filtering by batch correlation.\")\n\n    return genes_to_keep\n\ndef eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata: ad.AnnData) -> ad.AnnData:\n    \"\"\"\n    Applies advanced feature selection and then runs\
    \ the SOTA pipeline.\n    \"\"\"\n    print(\"--- Running Advanced Feature Selection + SOTA Graph ---\")\n\n    # Step 1: Select features using the new method\n    # Using default n_top_genes=2000, corr_threshold=0.1\n    robust_genes = get_union_features_batch_filtered(adata.copy())\n\n    # Step 2: Create a new AnnData object with only the selected features\n    adata_filtered = adata[:, robust_genes].copy()\n\n    # Step 3: Run the SOTA pipeline on the filtered data\n    print(f\"Running SOTA graph pipeline on {len(robust_genes)} selected features...\")\n    adata_result = run_sota_pipeline(adata_filtered)\n\n    # The SOTA pipeline returns an object with the reduced gene set.\n    # We need to return an object with the original 2000 genes for evaluation.\n    # Create a new adata object and copy the embedding and graph results.\n    final_adata = adata.copy()\n    final_adata.obsm['X_emb'] = adata_result.obsm['X_emb']\n    final_adata.obsp['connectivities'] = adata_result.obsp['connectivities']\n\
    \    final_adata.obsp['distances'] = adata_result.obsp['distances']\n\n    return final_adata\n\n```\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: python storage/system/main.py\nLoading training dataset...\n  Data shape: (20000, 2000)\n  Batches: 4 batches\nFound eliminate_batch_effect_fn, executing...\n\n=== Running batch integration ===\n--- Running Advanced Feature Selection + SOTA Graph ---\nFinding Union HVGs with Batch Correlation Filter...\nBatch Koenig et al. 2022: seurat_v3 successful\nBatch Kuppe et al. 2022: seurat_v3 successful\nBatch Litvinukova et al. 2020: seurat_v3 successful\nBatch Tucker et al. 2020: seurat_v3 successful\nSuccessfully processed 4/4 batches\nFound 2000 genes in the union of HVGs.\nWarning: Only 0 genes below correlation threshold 0.1\nKeeping top 1000 genes with lowest batch correlation instead\nKept 1000 genes after filtering by batch correlation.\nRunning SOTA graph pipeline on 1000 selected features...\n[best-k50]\
    \ lam=0.605, delta=0.10, kd=22, k=50\n  Result shape: (20000, 2000)\n  Has embedding: True\n  Has graph: True\n\nResult saved to: storage/shared/tmp/69f0c47c-8d9a-4044-a7ef-7beda306dddc/result_human.h5ad\n\nRESULT_UUID: 69f0c47c-8d9a-4044-a7ef-7beda306dddc\n\n\nSTDERR:\n\n```\n### Message 2\n\n**Automatic System Tips**\nDo not give up on an approach too easily. Implementation details are often the key—tweaking hyperparameters and other specifics may be enough to make an existing method work effectively.\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `storage read daedalus/idea_batch_robust_hvg.py` (in Research Counter);\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- File content for daedalus/idea_batch_robust_hvg.py will be displayed below.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | Single-cell RNA-seq Batch Integration |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running\
