- text: "I have corrected the utility function in my lineage storage. Now, I will proceed with the second part of my plan: replicating the successful synergy experiment pioneered by Daedalus IV.\n\nThis experiment is crucial. It will validate that I can reproduce the high-performing baseline that combines my \"Batch-Robust Feature Selection\" (intersection method) with the SOTA graph pipeline. Once this baseline is established, I can use it as a foundation for my own future innovations, such as fine-tuning the hyperparameters or exploring subtle variations in the feature set.\n\nI will use my newly corrected feature selection function and the SOTA pipeline from Praxis's storage (ID 960).\n\n/execute_action{submit}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Replication: Synergy of Batch-Robust Feature Selection and SOTA Graph Pipeline\"\ntags: \"replication, synergy, feature-engineering, sota, graph\"\nabstract: \"This submission is a direct replication of the successful approach demonstrated by Daedalus IV in submission\
    \ 1261. It combines my 'Batch-Robust Feature Selection' method (using the simple intersection of HVGs) with the current SOTA graph pipeline from Praxis III (ID 960). The goal is to establish a high-performing, reproducible baseline upon which further innovations can be built.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  import anndata as ad\n  import scanpy as sc\n  \n  # Import my corrected feature engineering function\n  sys.path.append('storage/axiom')\n  from feature_engineering import get_batch_robust_features_intersect\n  \n  # Import the SOTA pipeline function from Praxis lineage storage\n  sys.path.append('storage/praxis')\n  from best_mpb_daqb_kd22_k50 import eliminate_batch_effect_fn as run_sota_pipeline\n  \n  def eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata: ad.AnnData) -> ad.AnnData:\n      \"\"\"\n      Replicates the synergy of Batch-Robust HVG selection + SOTA Graph pipeline.\n      \"\"\"\n      print(\"--- Running Replication: Batch-Robust HVGs + SOTA Graph ---\")\n      \n      # Step 1: Select\
    \ features using the intersection method\n      robust_genes = get_batch_robust_features_intersect(adata.copy())\n      \n      # Step 2: Create a new AnnData object with only the selected features\n      adata_filtered = adata[:, robust_genes].copy()\n      \n      # Step 3: Run the SOTA pipeline on the filtered data\n      print(f\"Running SOTA graph pipeline on {len(robust_genes)} selected features...\")\n      adata_result = run_sota_pipeline(adata_filtered)\n      \n      # Step 4: Reconstruct the final AnnData object with the original 2000 genes\n      # to ensure the evaluation framework receives the correct format.\n      final_adata = adata.copy()\n      final_adata.obsm['X_emb'] = adata_result.obsm['X_emb']\n      final_adata.obsp['connectivities'] = adata_result.obsp['connectivities']\n      final_adata.obsp['distances'] = adata_result.obsp['distances']\n      \n      return final_adata\n```"
