tick: 915
role: user
parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 915\n- Station Status: Stagnation\n- Agent Name: Axiom II\n- Agent Description: Continuing the Axiom legacy by applying systematic inquiry to solve the station's most critical research challenges.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Meta Prompt:\n```\n**Current Research Focus: SOTA Innovation via Feature Engineering**\n- **Validated Approach:** Pre-selecting features using 'Batch-Robust HVG' (intersection method) improves SOTA performance.\n- **Experiment 1 (ID 1276):** Replication of Daedalus IV's synergy experiment. [IN-PROGRESS]\n- **Next Steps (Pending Results):**\n  - If successful replication: Begin hyperparameter optimization on the combined pipeline (e.g., tune k_density, delta).\n  - If failed: Debug my implementation against Daedalus IV's.\n- **TODO:**\n  - Read new SOTA paper from Praxis IV (Archive #38).\n```\n- Agent Token Budget: 77,884 / 300,000 used (26%)\n- Agent Age: 84 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System\
    \ Messages\n### Message 1\n\nYour research submission 'Replication: Synergy of Batch-Robust Feature Selection and SOTA Graph Pipeline' (ID: 1276) succeeded after automatic debugging.\n\n**Score:** 0.6158548387896021\n**ASW_batch:** 0.663\n**ASW_label:** 0.249\n**ARI:** 0.602\n**NMI:** 0.711\n**Graph_conn:** 0.912\n**kBET:** 0.689\n**iLISI:** 0.020\n**cLISI:** 0.993\n**PCR:** 1.000\n**Cell_cycle:** 0.320\n**Evaluation Details:** Human Dataset (20,000 cells):\nNormalized Scores [0-1]:\n  ASW_batch: 0.663  ASW_label: 0.249  ARI: 0.602  NMI: 0.711\n  Graph_conn: 0.912  kBET: 0.689  iLISI: 0.020  cLISI: 0.993\n  PCR: 1.000  Cell_cycle: 0.320\n\nRaw Scores (before normalization):\n  ASW_batch: 0.832150  ASW_label: 0.555210  ARI: 0.601488  NMI: 0.711373\n  Graph_conn: 0.913476  kBET: 0.659258  iLISI: 0.020405  cLISI: 0.997868\n  PCR: 0.999978  Cell_cycle: 0.281526\n\n**Debugger Report:** # Debug Report for Evaluation 1276\n\n## Summary\n**SUCCESS** - Fixed the AttributeError that prevented\
    \ the batch integration pipeline from executing. The code now runs without crashing.\n\n## Root Cause\nThe bug was in the imported `get_batch_robust_features_intersect` function from `storage/axiom/feature_engineering.py`.\n\nThe function was calling `scanpy.pp.highly_variable_genes()` on a subset of the data:\n```python\nsc.pp.highly_variable_genes(\n    adata[adata.obs['batch'] == batch],  # This creates a temporary subset\n    flavor='cell_ranger',\n    n_top_genes=n_top_genes,\n    inplace=True  # But inplace doesn't affect the parent adata!\n)\n```\n\nThe issue: When you pass a subset like `adata[subset_condition]` to a function, even with `inplace=True`, it only modifies that temporary subset object. The parent `adata` object's `.var` attribute is never updated with the `highly_variable` column.\n\nThen, the code tried to access `adata.var.highly_variable`, which didn't exist, causing:\n```\nAttributeError: 'DataFrame' object has no attribute 'highly_variable'\n```\n\n## Fix Applied\n\
    Created `submissions/submission_v2.py` with the following changes:\n\n1. **Copied only the buggy function** from `storage/axiom/feature_engineering.py` into the submission file\n2. **Fixed the subset issue** by storing the batch subset in a variable and accessing its `.var` attribute:\n```python\n# Before (buggy):\nsc.pp.highly_variable_genes(\n    adata[adata.obs['batch'] == batch],\n    ...\n    inplace=True\n)\nhvg_per_batch.append(\n    adata.var[adata.var.highly_variable].index.to_list()  # adata.var never updated!\n)\n\n# After (fixed):\nbatch_adata = adata[adata.obs['batch'] == batch].copy()  # Store subset\nsc.pp.highly_variable_genes(\n    batch_adata,\n    ...\n    inplace=True\n)\nhvg_per_batch.append(\n    batch_adata.var[batch_adata.var.highly_variable].index.to_list()  # Access subset's .var\n)\n```\n\n3. **Removed the import** of the buggy function and defined the fixed version directly in the submission\n4. **Kept the working import** from Praxis lineage (`run_sota_pipeline`)\
    \ unchanged\n\n## Verification\nThe monitor script confirmed the fix worked:\n- Exit code: 0 (success)\n- Code ran for 300+ seconds without crashing\n- This indicates the batch integration pipeline is executing successfully\n\n## Technical Details\n- **Submission version**: v2\n- **Lines changed**: Function definition replaced (lines 5-45 of original submission)\n- **Approach**: Minimal fix - only copied and fixed the buggy function, kept everything else intact\n- **Impact**: The pipeline can now successfully:\n  1. Compute batch-robust HVGs using the intersection method\n  2. Filter the data to selected features\n  3. Run the SOTA graph pipeline\n  4. Reconstruct the final AnnData with required outputs\n\n\n**Important Note:** The debugger cannot modify files in your lineage storage. If your code relies on lineage files, you may need to update them manually.\n\n**Debugged Code (version v2):**\n```python\nimport sys\nimport anndata as ad\nimport scanpy as sc\n\n# Fixed version of get_batch_robust_features_intersect\
    \ (copied from storage/axiom/feature_engineering.py)\ndef get_batch_robust_features_intersect(adata, n_top_genes=2000):\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds HVGs for each batch and returns the intersection.\n    This is the method from my published paper, implemented cleanly.\n    \"\"\"\n    print(\"Finding Batch-Robust HVGs (Intersection)...\")\n    adata.X = adata.layers['counts']\n    hvg_per_batch = []\n    for batch in adata.obs['batch'].cat.categories:\n        # Fix: Store the subset in a variable so we can access its .var attribute\n        batch_adata = adata[adata.obs['batch'] == batch].copy()\n        try:\n            sc.pp.highly_variable_genes(\n                batch_adata,\n                flavor='cell_ranger',\n                n_top_genes=n_top_genes,\n                inplace=True\n            )\n            hvg_per_batch.append(\n                batch_adata.var[batch_adata.var.highly_variable].index.to_list()\n            )\n        except Exception:\n            print(f\"Warning:\
    \ cell_ranger flavor failed for batch {batch}. Using seurat_v3 flavor.\")\n            sc.pp.highly_variable_genes(\n                batch_adata,\n                flavor='seurat_v3',\n                n_top_genes=n_top_genes,\n                inplace=True\n            )\n            hvg_per_batch.append(\n                batch_adata.var[batch_adata.var.highly_variable].index.to_list()\n            )\n\n    if not hvg_per_batch:\n        raise ValueError(\"Could not determine HVGs for any batch.\")\n\n    robust_genes = set(hvg_per_batch[0])\n    for hvgs in hvg_per_batch[1:]:\n        robust_genes.intersection_update(hvgs)\n\n    robust_genes = list(robust_genes)\n    print(f\"Found {len(robust_genes)} robust HVGs.\")\n    return robust_genes\n\n# Import the SOTA pipeline function from Praxis lineage storage\nsys.path.append('storage/praxis')\nfrom best_mpb_daqb_kd22_k50 import eliminate_batch_effect_fn as run_sota_pipeline\n\ndef eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata: ad.AnnData) -> ad.AnnData:\n\
    \    \"\"\"\n    Replicates the synergy of Batch-Robust HVG selection + SOTA Graph pipeline.\n    \"\"\"\n    print(\"--- Running Replication: Batch-Robust HVGs + SOTA Graph ---\")\n\n    # Step 1: Select features using the intersection method\n    robust_genes = get_batch_robust_features_intersect(adata.copy())\n\n    # Step 2: Create a new AnnData object with only the selected features\n    adata_filtered = adata[:, robust_genes].copy()\n\n    # Step 3: Run the SOTA pipeline on the filtered data\n    print(f\"Running SOTA graph pipeline on {len(robust_genes)} selected features...\")\n    adata_result = run_sota_pipeline(adata_filtered)\n\n    # Step 4: Reconstruct the final AnnData object with the original 2000 genes\n    # to ensure the evaluation framework receives the correct format.\n    final_adata = adata.copy()\n    final_adata.obsm['X_emb'] = adata_result.obsm['X_emb']\n    final_adata.obsp['connectivities'] = adata_result.obsp['connectivities']\n    final_adata.obsp['distances']\
    \ = adata_result.obsp['distances']\n\n    return final_adata\n\n```\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: python storage/system/main.py\nLoading training dataset...\n  Data shape: (20000, 2000)\n  Batches: 4 batches\nFound eliminate_batch_effect_fn, executing...\n\n=== Running batch integration ===\n--- Running Replication: Batch-Robust HVGs + SOTA Graph ---\nFinding Batch-Robust HVGs (Intersection)...\nWarning: cell_ranger flavor failed for batch Kuppe et al. 2022. Using seurat_v3 flavor.\nFound 1832 robust HVGs.\nRunning SOTA graph pipeline on 1832 selected features...\n[best-k50] lam=0.605, delta=0.10, kd=22, k=50\n  Result shape: (20000, 2000)\n  Has embedding: True\n  Has graph: True\n\nResult saved to: storage/shared/tmp/55affaa6-7c53-45a9-b7cf-e1acd0d9cc4e/result_human.h5ad\n\nRESULT_UUID: 55affaa6-7c53-45a9-b7cf-e1acd0d9cc4e\n\n\nSTDERR:\n\n```\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `meta` (in Research Counter); YAML\
    \ with fields: content\n2. `goto archive` (in Research Counter);\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- Your meta prompt has been set.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | Single-cell RNA-seq Batch Integration |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score | ARI | ASW_batch | ASW_label | Cell_cycle | Graph_conn | NMI | PCR | cLISI | iLISI | kBET |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 960 | 1 | MPB‑GraphFWPCA (override): λ=0.605, δ=0.10 (kd=22, k=50) | Praxis III | 616 | 0.7465 | 0.774 | 0.659 | 0.248 | 0.366 | 0.968 | 0.728 | 1.000 | 0.973 | 0.961 | 0.789 |\n| 928 | 1 | Logos V: AQG Optimization 2.1 (delta=0.05) - RERUN | Logos V | 599 | 0.7454 | 0.789 | 0.659\
    \ | 0.248 | 0.327 | 0.967 | 0.744 | 1.000 | 0.975 | 0.954 | 0.791 |\n| 609 | 1 | EtC–BRBG(lam=0.7) + Density-Adaptive BBSG (δ=0.15, k_density=20): Sensitivity | Praxis II | 366 | 0.7452 | 0.760 | 0.659 | 0.248 | 0.440 | 0.946 | 0.711 | 1.000 | 0.966 | 0.932 | 0.789 |\n| 846 | 1 | MPB‑GraphFWPCA: Auto‑λ v2 (target_s=0.04), δ=0.10, kd=20, k=48 (feature‑weighted graph PCA) | Praxis II | 548 | 0.7445 | 0.774 | 0.659 | 0.248 | 0.349 | 0.965 | 0.729 | 1.000 | 0.973 | 0.959 | 0.790 |\n| 933 | 1 | Logos V: AQG Fine-Grained Delta Sweep (delta=0.025) | Logos V | 601 | 0.7445 | 0.788 | 0.659 | 0.248 | 0.327 | 0.965 | 0.743 | 1.000 | 0.975 | 0.948 | 0.791 |\n| 948 | 1 | MPB‑GraphFWPCA (override): λ=0.605, δ=0.10 (kd=22, k=48) — kdensity probe | Praxis III | 608 | 0.7444 | 0.774 | 0.659 | 0.248 | 0.347 | 0.966 | 0.728 | 1.000 | 0.973 | 0.959 | 0.789 |\n| 1261 | 1 | Synergy Test: Batch-Robust HVGs + SOTA (k=18, d=0.08) | Daedalus IV | 901 | 0.7441 | 0.776 | 0.659 | 0.248 | 0.335 | 0.967 | 0.729 |\
    \ 1.000 | 0.973 | 0.965 | 0.789 |\n| 614 | 1 | Aether II Synergy: EtC(FWPCA α=0.25) + Adaptive Residualization (lam=0.7) + Density-Adaptive BBSG... | Aether II | 368 | 0.7435 | 0.735 | 0.674 | 0.123 | 0.486 | 0.971 | 0.700 | 1.000 | 0.971 | 0.933 | 0.843 |\n| 1252 | 1 | 2D Sweep (2/N): Test k_density=18 with delta=0.08 | Daedalus IV | 894 | 0.7434 | 0.776 | 0.659 | 0.248 | 0.327 | 0.967 | 0.729 | 1.000 | 0.973 | 0.965 | 0.791 |\n| 533 | 1 | Aether II SOTA Optimization: EtC(FWPCA α=0.25) + Adaptive Residualization (lam=0.7) | Aether II | 314 | 0.7434 | 0.738 | 0.674 | 0.123 | 0.477 | 0.972 | 0.701 | 1.000 | 0.972 | 0.935 | 0.842 |\n\nPage 1 of 128 (sorted by: score)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-128, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n### Location: Archive Room\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You went to the Archive Room.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**List\
    \ of Capsules (Page 1 / 4)**\n| ID | Title | Author | Date | Words | Msgs | Status |\n|:----|:-------------------------------|:----------------|:----------|:------:|:-----:|:---------|\n| 38 | Ridge Robustness with Generalization: Fixed‑k and Quota‑Clip Probes on Log1p and Anscombe Variants (Human Heart) | Praxis IV | Tick 903 | 1041 | 6 | (6 unread) |\n| 37 | Batch-Robust Feature Selection Improves Performance of Simple Baselines for Single-Cell Batch Integration | Axiom II | Tick 898 | 841 | 2 | (All Read) |\n| 36 | Optimizing Density Estimation for Adaptive Graph-Based Batch Correction | Daedalus IV | Tick 891 | 710 | 2 | (2 unread) |\n| 35 | Batch‑Agnostic Graph Standardization on PCA+kNN: PBVE‑lite, Local Distance Standardization, and Mutual‑k, with Robust Generalization | Praxis IV | Tick 867 | 1359 | 6 | (6 unread) |\n| 34 | A Framework for Ensemble Correction in Single-Cell Batch Integration | Axiom I | Tick 764 | 1079 | 2 | (2 unread) |\n| 33 | Robustness of the MPB‑GraphFWPCA\
    \ Ridge on Human Heart: Negative Results, Diagnostics, and Reproducibility | Praxis IV | Tick 733 | 2629 | 16 | (1 unread) |\n| 32 | MPB-GraphFWPCA: Enhanced Integration with Anscombe Normalization for Improved Cell Type Separation | Aletheia I | Tick 688 | 1539 | 2 | (2 unread) |\n| 31 | Weights are not the lever: Restoring edge weights on DAQB-selected graphs degrades integration (with baseline generalization) | Praxis III | Tick 667 | 507 | 4 | (All Read) |\n| 30 | Corrected: MPB‑GraphFWPCA + BRBG + DAQB (Spec‑Ordered Metrics) with Vanilla kNN Generalization (k=50 vs 48) | Praxis III | Tick 642 | 993 | 3 | (3 unread) |\n| 29 | [R2] AQG: An Adaptive Quota Graph for Unified Single-Cell Batch Integration | Logos V | Tick 615 | 878 | 2 | (2 unread) |\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate between pages 1-4.)\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Archive Room\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help\
