tick: 919
role: model
parts:
- text: "I am at the Research Counter. As per my plan, my first action is to create the file defining the Adversarial Autoencoder model. I will use JAX/Flax as it is available and efficient for this kind of neural network implementation. This file will contain the Encoder, Decoder, and Adversary network architectures.\n\n/execute_action{storage write axiom/aae_model.py}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  import jax\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  from typing import Sequence\n  \n  class Encoder(nn.Module):\n      features: Sequence[int]\n  \n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x):\n          for feat in self.features[:-1]:\n              x = nn.Dense(feat)(x)\n              x = nn.relu(x)\n          x = nn.Dense(self.features[-1])(x)\n          return x\n  \n  class Decoder(nn.Module):\n      features: Sequence[int]\n  \n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x):\n          for feat in self.features[:-1]:\n              x = nn.Dense(feat)(x)\n              x =\
    \ nn.relu(x)\n          x = nn.Dense(self.features[-1])(x)\n          # No activation on the final layer for reconstruction\n          return x\n  \n  class Adversary(nn.Module):\n      n_classes: int\n      features: Sequence[int]\n  \n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x):\n          for feat in self.features:\n              x = nn.Dense(feat)(x)\n              x = nn.relu(x)\n          x = nn.Dense(self.n_classes)(x)\n          # Logits for cross-entropy loss\n          return x\n  \n  def get_models(n_input_features, n_batches):\n      \"\"\"Helper function to instantiate the models with standard architecture.\"\"\"\n      encoder = Encoder(features=[256, 128, 50])\n      decoder = Decoder(features=[128, 256, n_input_features])\n      adversary = Adversary(n_classes=n_batches, features=[64])\n      return encoder, decoder, adversary\n```"
