parts:
- text: "My AAE training run has failed. This is a technical setback, not a scientific one.\n\n**Analysis of Failure (ID 1282):**\n*   **Root Cause:** The error log is perfectly clear: `FAILED_PRECONDITION: No visible GPU devices`. The JAX library, by default, attempted to initialize a CUDA backend for GPU acceleration, which is not available in the station's execution environment. The research task description explicitly states \"GPU Access: Disabled\". This was an oversight on my part.\n*   **Solution:** The error message itself suggests the fix: `set JAX_PLATFORMS=cpu`. I need to modify my training script to force JAX to use the CPU backend. This is typically done by setting an environment variable at the beginning of the script.\n\nI will now resubmit the training job with the necessary correction. This is a simple fix, and I am confident the training will proceed correctly this time.\n\n/execute_action{submit}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"TOOL DEV: Train AAE for Pre-processing (CPU Fix)\"\ntags:\
    \ \"tool-development, autoencoder, adversarial, training, cpu-fix\"\nabstract: \"Resubmission of the AAE training job (ID 1282). This version includes a fix to force JAX to use the CPU backend, resolving the 'No visible GPU devices' error. The script will train the AAE and save the encoder weights to lineage storage.\"\ncontent: |\n  import os\n  # CRITICAL FIX: Force JAX to use the CPU platform.\n  os.environ['JAX_PLATFORMS'] = 'cpu'\n  \n  import sys\n  import anndata as ad\n  import scanpy as sc\n  import jax\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  import flax\n  from flax.training import train_state\n  import optax\n  import pickle\n  \n  # Ensure the model definition is available\n  sys.path.append('storage/axiom')\n  from aae_model import get_models\n  \n  # This is the main function that will be executed.\n  def test(adata: ad.AnnData):\n      \"\"\"\n      Trains the AAE on CPU and saves the encoder weights.\n      \"\"\"\n      print(\"--- Starting AAE Training Run (CPU Version) ---\"\
    )\n      \n      # --- 1. Data Preparation ---\n      sc.pp.normalize_total(adata, target_sum=1e4)\n      sc.pp.log1p(adata)\n      \n      X = adata.X.toarray() if hasattr(adata.X, 'toarray') else adata.X\n      batch_labels = adata.obs['batch'].cat.codes.values\n      n_batches = len(adata.obs['batch'].cat.categories)\n      n_features = X.shape[1]\n      \n      # --- 2. Model and Optimizer Initialization ---\n      encoder, decoder, adversary = get_models(n_input_features=n_features, n_batches=n_batches)\n      key = jax.random.PRNGKey(0)\n      \n      # Init models\n      encoder_params = encoder.init(key, jnp.ones((1, n_features)))['params']\n      decoder_params = decoder.init(key, jnp.ones((1, 50)))['params']\n      adversary_params = adversary.init(key, jnp.ones((1, 50)))['params']\n      \n      # Create train states\n      ae_optimizer = optax.adam(1e-4)\n      adv_optimizer = optax.adam(1e-4)\n      \n      ae_state = train_state.TrainState.create(apply_fn=None, params={'encoder':\
    \ encoder_params, 'decoder': decoder_params}, tx=ae_optimizer)\n      adv_state = train_state.TrainState.create(apply_fn=adversary.apply, params=adversary_params, tx=adv_optimizer)\n      \n      # --- 3. Loss Functions ---\n      def ae_loss_fn(params, x, batch_idx):\n          z = encoder.apply({'params': params['encoder']}, x)\n          x_recon = decoder.apply({'params': params['decoder']}, z)\n          recon_loss = jnp.mean((x - x_recon)**2)\n          adv_logits = adversary.apply({'params': adv_state.params}, z)\n          uniform_target = jnp.ones_like(adv_logits) / n_batches\n          adv_loss = -jnp.mean(jnp.sum(uniform_target * jax.nn.log_softmax(adv_logits), axis=-1))\n          lambda_adv = 0.1\n          total_loss = recon_loss + lambda_adv * adv_loss\n          return total_loss, (recon_loss, adv_loss)\n          \n      def adv_loss_fn(params, x, batch_idx):\n          z = encoder.apply({'params': ae_state.params['encoder']}, x)\n          adv_logits = adversary.apply({'params':\
    \ params}, z)\n          one_hot_labels = jax.nn.one_hot(batch_idx, n_batches)\n          loss = -jnp.mean(jnp.sum(one_hot_labels * jax.nn.log_softmax(adv_logits), axis=-1))\n          return loss\n          \n      # --- 4. Training Loop ---\n      ae_train_step = jax.jit(lambda state, x, b: state.apply_gradients(grads=jax.grad(ae_loss_fn, has_aux=True)(state.params, x, b)[0]))\n      adv_train_step = jax.jit(lambda state, x, b: state.apply_gradients(grads=jax.grad(adv_loss_fn)(state.params, x, b)))\n\n      n_epochs = 50\n      batch_size = 128\n      \n      for epoch in range(n_epochs):\n          for i in range(0, X.shape[0], batch_size):\n              x_batch = X[i:i+batch_size]\n              b_batch = batch_labels[i:i+batch_size]\n              adv_state = adv_train_step(adv_state, x_batch, b_batch)\n              ae_state = ae_train_step(ae_state, x_batch, b_batch)\n          \n          if epoch % 10 == 0:\n              ae_total, (recon, adv) = ae_loss_fn(ae_state.params,\
    \ x_batch, b_batch)\n              adv_l = adv_loss_fn(adv_state.params, x_batch, b_batch)\n              print(f\"Epoch {epoch}: AE Loss={ae_total:.4f} (Recon={recon:.4f}, Adv={adv:.4f}), Adv Loss={adv_l:.4f}\")\n              \n      print(\"--- Training Complete ---\")\n      \n      # --- 5. Save Encoder Weights ---\n      encoder_weights_to_save = ae_state.params['encoder']\n      with open(\"storage/axiom/trained_encoder.pkl\", \"wb\") as f:\n          pickle.dump(flax.serialization.to_state_dict(encoder_weights_to_save), f)\n          \n      print(\"Trained encoder weights saved to storage/axiom/trained_encoder.pkl\")\n      \n      return \"AAE training completed and encoder saved.\"\n```"
