tick: 922
role: model
parts:
- text: "Excellent. The AAE training run (ID 1283) has completed successfully. The log shows that the training progressed as expected, and the final message confirms that the trained encoder weights have been saved to `storage/axiom/trained_encoder.pkl`. Phase 1 of my plan is complete.\n\nNow I move to Phase 2: submitting the formal experiment that uses this pre-trained encoder.\n\nMy hypothesis remains that feeding a non-linear, batch-corrected latent embedding from my AAE into the SOTA graph algorithm will yield a breakthrough performance. The submission script will load the saved encoder, transform the input data into the latent representation, and then pass this representation to the graph-building stage of the SOTA pipeline.\n\nA critical implementation detail is that the SOTA pipeline's function (`run_sota_pipeline`) performs PCA internally. I must bypass this. The easiest way is to create a dummy `AnnData` object where the `.X` attribute is my 50-dimensional latent embedding. When\
    \ the SOTA pipeline runs `sc.tl.pca()` on this, it will effectively be doing a PCA on my already-low-dimensional embedding, which is a reasonable way to pass the data into its k-NN graph construction step without major code surgery.\n\nI will now submit this final experiment.\n\n/execute_action{submit}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"SOTA Graph on Adversarial Autoencoder Latent Space\"\ntags: \"autoencoder, adversarial, sota, graph, pre-processing, non-linear\"\nabstract: \"This experiment tests a novel pre-processing method for the SOTA graph pipeline. We use a pre-trained Adversarial Autoencoder (AAE) to generate a 50-dimensional latent embedding of the data, designed to be batch-invariant while preserving biological structure. This embedding is then used as the direct input for the SOTA graph construction algorithm, bypassing its standard PCA step. The hypothesis is that this superior, non-linear, batch-corrected input representation will enable the SOTA algorithm to overcome its known 'mixing\
    \ shortfall' and achieve a new SOTA score.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  import anndata as ad\n  import scanpy as sc\n  import jax\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  import flax\n  import pickle\n  \n  # Set JAX to CPU\n  import os\n  os.environ['JAX_PLATFORMS'] = 'cpu'\n  \n  # Import model definitions and SOTA pipeline\n  sys.path.append('storage/axiom')\n  from aae_model import get_models\n  sys.path.append('storage/praxis')\n  from best_mpb_daqb_kd22_k50 import eliminate_batch_effect_fn as run_sota_pipeline\n  \n  def eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata: ad.AnnData) -> ad.AnnData:\n      \"\"\"\n      Generates AAE embedding and runs the SOTA graph pipeline on it.\n      \"\"\"\n      print(\"--- Running SOTA Graph on AAE Latent Space ---\")\n      \n      # --- 1. Load Pre-trained Encoder ---\n      n_features = adata.shape[1]\n      n_batches = len(adata.obs['batch'].cat.categories)\n      encoder, _, _ = get_models(n_input_features=n_features, n_batches=n_batches)\n      \n      with\
    \ open(\"storage/axiom/trained_encoder.pkl\", \"rb\") as f:\n          encoder_params = pickle.load(f)\n      \n      encoder_params = flax.serialization.from_state_dict(encoder.init(jax.random.PRNGKey(0), jnp.ones((1, n_features)))['params'], encoder_params)\n      \n      # --- 2. Prepare Data and Generate Embedding ---\n      adata_norm = adata.copy()\n      sc.pp.normalize_total(adata_norm, target_sum=1e4)\n      sc.pp.log1p(adata_norm)\n      X_norm = adata_norm.X.toarray() if hasattr(adata_norm.X, 'toarray') else adata_norm.X\n      \n      print(\"Generating latent embedding from pre-trained encoder...\")\n      latent_embedding = encoder.apply({'params': encoder_params}, X_norm)\n      print(f\"Generated embedding of shape: {latent_embedding.shape}\")\n      \n      # --- 3. Run SOTA Pipeline on the Latent Embedding ---\n      # Create a new AnnData object for the pipeline.\n      # The SOTA function expects HVG info and batch labels.\n      adata_latent = ad.AnnData(latent_embedding)\n\
    \      adata_latent.obs['batch'] = adata.obs['batch'].values\n      # The SOTA pipeline uses `adata.var['highly_variable']`, so we must set it.\n      # For the latent space, all 50 features are considered 'highly_variable'.\n      adata_latent.var['highly_variable'] = True\n      \n      print(\"Running SOTA graph pipeline on the AAE embedding...\")\n      # This will run PCA on our 50-dim embedding, then build the graph.\n      adata_result_graph = run_sota_pipeline(adata_latent)\n      \n      # --- 4. Format Output ---\n      # The final result needs the original adata structure but with the new graph and embedding.\n      final_adata = adata.copy()\n      # The SOTA pipeline itself returns an embedding, which is a PCA of our AAE embedding.\n      final_adata.obsm['X_emb'] = adata_result_graph.obsm['X_emb']\n      final_adata.obsp['connectivities'] = adata_result_graph.obsp['connectivities']\n      final_adata.obsp['distances'] = adata_result_graph.obsp['distances']\n      \n   \
    \   return final_adata\n```"
