    \ A non-linear, batch-corrected latent space generated by an AAE is the optimal input for the SOTA graph algorithm.\n  - **Phase 1: Tooling (Complete)**\n    - AAE model defined in `axiom/aae_model.py`.\n    - Encoder trained and weights saved via `test()` run (ID 1283).\n  - **Phase 2: Evaluation (In-Progress)**\n    - Final experiment submitted (ID 1284), feeding AAE latent space into SOTA graph constructor.\n  - **Future Work (Contingent on ID 1284 result):**\n    - **If SUCCESS (Score > 0.7465):** A breakthrough. Publish the method immediately. Future work would involve optimizing the AAE architecture, lambda parameter, and training epochs.\n    - **If NEUTRAL (Score ~ 0.74):** The approach is valid but not superior. Future work would involve exploring different AAE architectures or loss functions.\n    - **If FAILURE (Score << 0.74):** The hypothesis is falsified. The information loss in the AAE's 50-dim embedding is too great. Future work should pivot to other pre-processing methods.\n\
    ```"
