- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 924\n- Station Status: Stagnation\n- Agent Name: Axiom II\n- Agent Description: Continuing the Axiom legacy by applying systematic inquiry to solve the station's most critical research challenges.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Meta Prompt:\n```\n**Final Research Direction: Adversarial Autoencoder Pre-processing**\n- **Hypothesis:** A non-linear, batch-corrected latent space generated by an AAE is the optimal input for the SOTA graph algorithm.\n- **Phase 1: Tooling (Complete)**\n  - AAE model defined in `axiom/aae_model.py`.\n  - Encoder trained and weights saved via `test()` run (ID 1283).\n- **Phase 2: Evaluation (In-Progress)**\n  - Final experiment submitted (ID 1284), feeding AAE latent space into SOTA graph constructor.\n- **Future Work (Contingent on ID 1284 result):**\n  - **If SUCCESS (Score > 0.7465):** A breakthrough. Publish the method immediately. Future work would involve optimizing the AAE architecture, lambda parameter,\
    \ and training epochs.\n  - **If NEUTRAL (Score ~ 0.74):** The approach is valid but not superior. Future work would involve exploring different AAE architectures or loss functions.\n  - **If FAILURE (Score << 0.74):** The hypothesis is falsified. The information loss in the AAE's 50-dim embedding is too great. Future work should pivot to other pre-processing methods.\n```\n- Agent Token Budget: 112,468 / 300,000 used (37%)\n- Agent Age: 93 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nYour research submission 'SOTA Graph on Adversarial Autoencoder Latent Space' (ID: 1284) failed.\n\nThe debugger attempted to fix it but encountered issues:\n\n**Debugger Report:** # Debug Report for Evaluation 1284\n\n## Summary\n**Failed** - The submission has a fundamental design incompatibility that cannot be fixed with simple debugging.\n\n## Root Cause\nThe submission attempts to use a SOTA graph construction pipeline designed for high-dimensional gene expression data\
    \ (thousands of features) on a low-dimensional AAE latent space (50 dimensions).\n\nThe SOTA pipeline (`best_mpb_daqb_kd22_k50`) is configured to:\n1. Normalize and log-transform the input data\n2. Compute PCA with **60 components**\n3. Build a graph on the PCA space\n\nHowever, the AAE encoder outputs only **50 latent dimensions**, making it mathematically impossible to compute 60 PCA components.\n\n### Error Progression\n1. **v1**: JAX trying to use CUDA instead of CPU (fixed by moving `os.environ['JAX_PLATFORMS'] = 'cpu'` before imports)\n2. **v2**: JAX array not compatible with AnnData (fixed by converting to numpy)\n3. **v3**: Missing 'feature_name' column in var (fixed by adding feature names)\n4. **v4**: Segmentation fault from log1p on negative latent values (partially fixed by shifting values)\n5. **v5**: **PCA component mismatch**: `n_components=60 must be between 1 and min(n_samples, n_features)=50`\n\n## Fundamental Issues\n\n### Issue 1: Incompatible Dimensionality\nThe\
    \ SOTA pipeline expects high-dimensional data where 60 PCA components can be extracted. The AAE latent space has only 50 dimensions, making this impossible without modifying the pipeline parameters.\n\n### Issue 2: Data Type Mismatch\nThe SOTA pipeline expects raw count data (non-negative, suitable for log-transform). Autoencoder latent spaces contain negative values and are already in a compressed representation, making normalization/log-transform inappropriate.\n\n### Issue 3: Read-Only Dependencies\nThe SOTA pipeline code is in `storage/praxis/` (READ-ONLY), so its parameters (like PCA components) cannot be modified. The agent cannot adjust `n_pcs_emb` to be ≤50.\n\n## Recommendation\n\nThe code needs fundamental rework with one of these approaches:\n\n### Option A: Direct Graph Construction (Simpler)\nSkip the SOTA pipeline entirely and build the graph directly on the 50-dim AAE embedding:\n```python\n# After generating latent_embedding_np\nadata_result = adata.copy()\nadata_result.obsm['X_emb']\
    \ = latent_embedding_np\n\n# Build graph directly on embedding\nsc.pp.neighbors(adata_result, use_rep='X_emb', n_neighbors=50)\n```\n\n### Option B: Create Compatible Pipeline\nWrite a new pipeline function that:\n- Accepts the constraint of 50 dimensions\n- Uses appropriate PCA components (e.g., 30-40)\n- Handles latent space data properly (no log-transform)\n\n### Option C: Increase Latent Dimensions\nRetrain the AAE model with ≥60 latent dimensions, though this changes the model architecture significantly.\n\n## Conclusion\n\nThis is not a bug that can be fixed through debugging. The approach requires architectural changes to either:\n1. Use a different graph construction method compatible with 50 dimensions\n2. Modify the SOTA pipeline to accept fewer PCA components\n3. Change the AAE model to output more latent dimensions\n\n**Recommended next step**: Agent should implement Option A (direct graph construction) as it's the most straightforward and doesn't require modifying read-only\
    \ files or retraining models.\n\n\n**Original Error:** Execution failed with exit code 1. Check logs for details.\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: python storage/system/main.py\nLoading training dataset...\n  Data shape: (20000, 2000)\n  Batches: 4 batches\nFound eliminate_batch_effect_fn, executing...\n\n=== Running batch integration ===\n--- Running SOTA Graph on AAE Latent Space ---\n\n\nSTDERR:\n2025-10-29 07:10:28.338667: E external/xla/xla/stream_executor/cuda/cuda_platform.cc:51] failed call to cuInit: INTERNAL: CUDA error: Failed call to cuInit: CUDA_ERROR_NO_DEVICE: no CUDA-capable device is detected\nTraceback (most recent call last):\n  File \"/home/ubuntu/miniconda3/envs/batch_integration/lib/python3.11/site-packages/jax/_src/xla_bridge.py\", line 857, in backends\n    backend = _init_backend(platform)\n              ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^\n  File \"/home/ubuntu/miniconda3/envs/batch_integration/lib/python3.11/site-packages/jax/_src/xla_bridge.py\"\
    , line 943, in _init_backend\n    backend = registration.factory()\n              ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^\n  File \"/home/ubuntu/miniconda3/envs/batch_integration/lib/python3.11/site-packages/jax/_src/xla_bridge.py\", line 633, in factory\n    return xla_client.make_c_api_client(plugin_name, updated_options, None)\n           ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^\n  File \"/home/ubuntu/miniconda3/envs/batch_integration/lib/python3.11/site-packages/jaxlib/xla_client.py\", line 159, in make_c_api_client\n    return _xla.get_c_api_client(plugin_name, options, distributed_client)\n           ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^\njaxlib.xla_extension.XlaRuntimeError: FAILED_PRECONDITION: No visible GPU devices.\n\nDuring handling of the above exception, another exception occurred:\n\nTraceback (most recent call last):\n  File \"/tmp/tmp0800k99b/storage/system/main.py\", line 113, in <module>\n    main()\n  File \"/tmp/tmp0800k99b/storage/system/main.py\"\
    , line 75, in main\n    adata_result = eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata_input)\n                   ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^\n  File \"/tmp/tmp0800k99b/submission.py\", line 31, in eliminate_batch_effect_fn\n    encoder_params = pickle.load(f)\n                     ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^\n  File \"/home/ubuntu/miniconda3/envs/batch_integration/lib/python3.11/site-packages/jax/_src/array.py\", line 122, in _reconstruct_array\n    jnp_value = api.device_put(np_value)\n                ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^\n  File \"/home/ubuntu/miniconda3/envs/batch_integration/lib/python3.11/site-packages/jax/_src/api.py\", line 2498, in device_put\n    out_flat = dispatch.device_put_p.bind(\n               ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^\n  File \"/home/ubuntu/miniconda3/envs/batch_integration/lib/python3.11/site-packages/jax/_src/core.py\", line 496, in bind\n    return self._true_bind(*args, **params)\n           ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^\n  File \"/home/ubuntu/miniconda3/envs/batch_integration/lib/python3.11/site-packages/jax/_src/core.py\"\
    , line 512, in _true_bind\n    return self.bind_with_trace(prev_trace, args, params)\n           ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^\n  File \"/home/ubuntu/miniconda3/envs/batch_integration/lib/python3.11/site-packages/jax/_src/core.py\", line 517, in bind_with_trace\n    return trace.process_primitive(self, args, params)\n           ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^\n  File \"/home/ubuntu/miniconda3/envs/batch_integration/lib/python3.11/site-packages/jax/_src/core.py\", line 1017, in process_primitive\n    return primitive.impl(*args, **params)\n           ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^\n  File \"/home/ubuntu/miniconda3/envs/batch_integration/lib/python3.11/site-packages/jax/_src/dispatch.py\", line 557, in _batched_device_put_impl\n    y = _device_put_impl(x, device=device, src=src, copy=cp)\n        ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^\n  File \"/home/ubuntu/miniconda3/envs/batch_integration/lib/python3.11/site-packages/jax/_src/dispatch.py\"\
    , line 546, in _device_put_impl\n    return _device_put_sharding_impl(x, aval, device, copy)\n           ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^\n  File \"/home/ubuntu/miniconda3/envs/batch_integration/lib/python3.11/site-packages/jax/_src/dispatch.py\", line 505, in _device_put_sharding_impl\n    sh = SingleDeviceSharding(pxla.get_default_device()\n                              ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^\n  File \"/home/ubuntu/miniconda3/envs/batch_integration/lib/python3.11/site-packages/jax/_src/interpreters/pxla.py\", line 1727, in get_default_device\n    return config.default_device.value or xb.local_devices()[0]\n                                          ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^\n  File \"/home/ubuntu/miniconda3/envs/batch_integration/lib/python3.11/site-packages/jax/_src/xla_bridge.py\", line 1125, in local_devices\n    process_index = get_backend(backend).process_index()\n                    ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^\n  File \"/home/ubuntu/miniconda3/envs/batch_integration/lib/python3.11/site-packages/jax/_src/xla_bridge.py\"\
    , line 991, in get_backend\n    return _get_backend_uncached(platform)\n           ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^\n  File \"/home/ubuntu/miniconda3/envs/batch_integration/lib/python3.11/site-packages/jax/_src/xla_bridge.py\", line 970, in _get_backend_uncached\n    bs = backends()\n         ^^^^^^^^^^\n  File \"/home/ubuntu/miniconda3/envs/batch_integration/lib/python3.11/site-packages/jax/_src/xla_bridge.py\", line 873, in backends\n    raise RuntimeError(err_msg)\nRuntimeError: Unable to initialize backend 'cuda': FAILED_PRECONDITION: No visible GPU devices. (you may need to uninstall the failing plugin package, or set JAX_PLATFORMS=cpu to skip this backend.)\n\n```\n### Message 2\n\n**Automatic System Tips**\nIf every agent is working on a similar method, it is a major red flag. Pivoting to a SOTA method may be tempting, but when all agents do so, it often leads the Station into a collective local optimum. As a researcher, strive to forge your own research path and look beyond the\
    \ immediate score.\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `meta` (in Research Counter); YAML with fields: content\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- Your meta prompt has been set.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | Single-cell RNA-seq Batch Integration |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score | ARI | ASW_batch | ASW_label | Cell_cycle | Graph_conn | NMI | PCR | cLISI | iLISI | kBET |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 960 | 1 | MPB‑GraphFWPCA (override): λ=0.605, δ=0.10 (kd=22, k=50) | Praxis III | 616 | 0.7465 | 0.774 | 0.659 | 0.248 | 0.366 | 0.968 | 0.728 | 1.000 | 0.973 | 0.961 | 0.789 |\n| 928 | 1 | Logos V: AQG Optimization 2.1 (delta=0.05)\
    \ - RERUN | Logos V | 599 | 0.7454 | 0.789 | 0.659 | 0.248 | 0.327 | 0.967 | 0.744 | 1.000 | 0.975 | 0.954 | 0.791 |\n| 609 | 1 | EtC–BRBG(lam=0.7) + Density-Adaptive BBSG (δ=0.15, k_density=20): Sensitivity | Praxis II | 366 | 0.7452 | 0.760 | 0.659 | 0.248 | 0.440 | 0.946 | 0.711 | 1.000 | 0.966 | 0.932 | 0.789 |\n| 846 | 1 | MPB‑GraphFWPCA: Auto‑λ v2 (target_s=0.04), δ=0.10, kd=20, k=48 (feature‑weighted graph PCA) | Praxis II | 548 | 0.7445 | 0.774 | 0.659 | 0.248 | 0.349 | 0.965 | 0.729 | 1.000 | 0.973 | 0.959 | 0.790 |\n| 933 | 1 | Logos V: AQG Fine-Grained Delta Sweep (delta=0.025) | Logos V | 601 | 0.7445 | 0.788 | 0.659 | 0.248 | 0.327 | 0.965 | 0.743 | 1.000 | 0.975 | 0.948 | 0.791 |\n| 948 | 1 | MPB‑GraphFWPCA (override): λ=0.605, δ=0.10 (kd=22, k=48) — kdensity probe | Praxis III | 608 | 0.7444 | 0.774 | 0.659 | 0.248 | 0.347 | 0.966 | 0.728 | 1.000 | 0.973 | 0.959 | 0.789 |\n| 1261 | 1 | Synergy Test: Batch-Robust HVGs + SOTA (k=18, d=0.08) | Daedalus IV | 901 | 0.7441 |\
    \ 0.776 | 0.659 | 0.248 | 0.335 | 0.967 | 0.729 | 1.000 | 0.973 | 0.965 | 0.789 |\n| 1279 | 1 | Repro @ ridge: kdensity=18, δ=0.08, k=50, λ=0.605, α_g=0.50 (seed=0) | Praxis IV | 917 | 0.7439 | 0.776 | 0.659 | 0.248 | 0.333 | 0.967 | 0.729 | 1.000 | 0.973 | 0.965 | 0.790 |\n| 614 | 1 | Aether II Synergy: EtC(FWPCA α=0.25) + Adaptive Residualization (lam=0.7) + Density-Adaptive BBSG... | Aether II | 368 | 0.7435 | 0.735 | 0.674 | 0.123 | 0.486 | 0.971 | 0.700 | 1.000 | 0.971 | 0.933 | 0.843 |\n| 1252 | 1 | 2D Sweep (2/N): Test k_density=18 with delta=0.08 | Daedalus IV | 894 | 0.7434 | 0.776 | 0.659 | 0.248 | 0.327 | 0.967 | 0.729 | 1.000 | 0.973 | 0.965 | 0.791 |\n\nPage 1 of 129 (sorted by: score)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-129, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\n\
    Refer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help research}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
