parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 925\n- Station Status: Stagnation\n- Agent Name: Axiom II\n- Agent Description: Continuing the Axiom legacy by applying systematic inquiry to solve the station's most critical research challenges.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Meta Prompt:\n```\n**Final Research Direction: Adversarial Autoencoder Pre-processing**\n- **Hypothesis:** A non-linear, batch-corrected latent space generated by an AAE is the optimal input for the SOTA graph algorithm.\n- **Phase 1: Tooling (Complete)**\n  - AAE model defined in `axiom/aae_model.py`.\n  - Encoder trained and weights saved via `test()` run (ID 1283).\n- **Phase 2: Evaluation (In-Progress)**\n  - Final experiment submitted (ID 1284), feeding AAE latent space into SOTA graph constructor.\n- **Future Work (Contingent on ID 1284 result):**\n  - **If SUCCESS (Score > 0.7465):** A breakthrough. Publish the method immediately. Future work would involve optimizing the AAE architecture, lambda parameter,\
    \ and training epochs.\n  - **If NEUTRAL (Score ~ 0.74):** The approach is valid but not superior. Future work would involve exploring different AAE architectures or loss functions.\n  - **If FAILURE (Score << 0.74):** The hypothesis is falsified. The information loss in the AAE's 50-dim embedding is too great. Future work should pivot to other pre-processing methods.\n```\n- Agent Token Budget: 119,021 / 300,000 used (40%)\n- Agent Age: 94 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nYour submission has been queued for evaluation. Results will be sent to you once the evaluation completes.\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `submit` (in Research Counter); YAML with fields: title, tags, abstract, content\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- Evaluation 'Direct Graph Construction on AAE Latent Embedding' submitted for Research Task #1: Single-cell RNA-seq Batch Integration. Evaluation\
