    \  NMI: 0.601\n  Graph_conn: 0.921  kBET: 0.660  iLISI: 0.041  cLISI: 0.949\n  PCR: 0.000  Cell_cycle: 0.396\n\nRaw Scores (before normalization):\n  ASW_batch: 0.800080  ASW_label: 0.501162  ARI: 0.379529  NMI: 0.601140\n  Graph_conn: 0.922190  kBET: 0.631836  iLISI: 0.041090  cLISI: 0.985212\n  PCR: 0.000000  Cell_cycle: 0.346756\n\n**Debugger Report:** # Debug Report for Evaluation 1289\n\n## Summary\n**SUCCESS** - Fixed the submission code. The algorithm now runs without crashing and has been executing for over 300 seconds.\n\n## Root Cause\nThe original submission had two critical bugs:\n\n1. **JAX Platform Configuration Timing Issue**: The code set `os.environ['JAX_PLATFORMS'] = 'cpu'` AFTER importing JAX and other libraries. When `pickle.load()` was called to load the pre-trained encoder parameters, JAX tried to initialize the CUDA backend during array reconstruction, which failed because no GPU was available in the sandbox environment.\n\n2. **Type Incompatibility with AnnData**:\
    \ The latent embedding generated by the encoder was a JAX array (`jaxlib.xla_extension.ArrayImpl`), but AnnData's `obsm` attribute only accepts specific types like NumPy arrays, SciPy sparse matrices, etc. Attempting to assign the JAX array directly caused a `ValueError`.\n\n## Fix Applied\n\n### Version 2 - Fixed JAX Platform Configuration\nMoved the JAX platform configuration to the very beginning of the file, BEFORE any imports:\n\n```python\n# Set JAX to CPU BEFORE any imports\nimport os\nos.environ['JAX_PLATFORMS'] = 'cpu'\n\nimport sys\nimport anndata as ad\nimport scanpy as sc\nimport jax\n...\n```\n\nThis ensures that when JAX is imported and when `pickle.load()` reconstructs JAX arrays, it uses the CPU backend instead of trying to initialize CUDA.\n\n**Result**: Fixed the CUDA initialization error, but revealed a new type incompatibility issue.\n\n### Version 3 - Fixed Type Incompatibility\nAdded NumPy import and converted the JAX array to NumPy before assigning to AnnData:\n\
    \n```python\nimport numpy as np\n...\n# Convert JAX array to NumPy array before assigning to obsm\nadata_result.obsm['X_emb'] = np.array(latent_embedding)\n```\n\n**Result**: Code now runs successfully without crashes. The algorithm successfully:\n- Loads the pre-trained encoder\n- Generates latent embeddings from the input data\n- Builds a k-NN graph on the latent space\n- Returns the processed AnnData object\n\n## Verification\nThe monitor script confirmed that submission_v3.py has been running for over 300 seconds without errors, indicating the code is working correctly. The evaluation is still running, which is expected for a batch integration task processing 20,000 cells with 2,000 features.\n\n\n**Important Note:** The debugger cannot modify files in your lineage storage. If your code relies on lineage files, you may need to update them manually.\n\n**Debugged Code (version v3):**\n```python\n# Set JAX to CPU BEFORE any imports\nimport os\nos.environ['JAX_PLATFORMS'] = 'cpu'\n\n\
    import sys\nimport anndata as ad\nimport scanpy as sc\nimport jax\nimport jax.numpy as jnp\nimport flax\nimport pickle\nimport numpy as np\n\n# Import model definitions\nsys.path.append('storage/axiom')\nfrom aae_model import get_models\n\ndef eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata: ad.AnnData) -> ad.AnnData:\n    \"\"\"\n    Generates AAE embedding and builds a k-NN graph directly on it.\n    \"\"\"\n    print(\"--- Running Direct Graph Construction on AAE Latent Space ---\")\n\n    # --- 1. Load Pre-trained Encoder ---\n    n_features = adata.shape[1]\n    n_batches = len(adata.obs['batch'].cat.categories)\n    encoder, _, _ = get_models(n_input_features=n_features, n_batches=n_batches)\n\n    with open(\"storage/axiom/trained_encoder.pkl\", \"rb\") as f:\n        encoder_params = pickle.load(f)\n\n    # Re-initialize the model structure before loading state dict\n    key = jax.random.PRNGKey(0)\n    initial_params = encoder.init(key, jnp.ones((1, n_features)))['params']\n    encoder_params\
    \ = flax.serialization.from_state_dict(initial_params, encoder_params)\n\n    # --- 2. Prepare Data and Generate Embedding ---\n    adata_norm = adata.copy()\n    sc.pp.normalize_total(adata_norm, target_sum=1e4)\n    sc.pp.log1p(adata_norm)\n    X_norm = adata_norm.X.toarray() if hasattr(adata_norm.X, 'toarray') else adata_norm.X\n\n    print(\"Generating latent embedding from pre-trained encoder...\")\n    latent_embedding = encoder.apply({'params': encoder_params}, X_norm)\n    print(f\"Generated embedding of shape: {latent_embedding.shape}\")\n\n    # --- 3. Build Graph Directly on the Latent Embedding ---\n    adata_result = adata.copy()\n    # Convert JAX array to NumPy array before assigning to obsm\n    adata_result.obsm['X_emb'] = np.array(latent_embedding)\n\n    print(\"Building k-NN graph directly on the AAE embedding...\")\n    # Use a standard neighbor count, similar to the SOTA baseline\n    sc.pp.neighbors(adata_result, use_rep='X_emb', n_neighbors=50)\n\n    # The embedding\
    \ itself is also a valid output for evaluation\n    # The evaluation metrics will use the graph if present, which it is.\n\n    return adata_result\n\n```\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: python storage/system/main.py\nLoading training dataset...\n  Data shape: (20000, 2000)\n  Batches: 4 batches\nFound eliminate_batch_effect_fn, executing...\n\n=== Running batch integration ===\n--- Running Direct Graph Construction on AAE Latent Space ---\nGenerating latent embedding from pre-trained encoder...\nGenerated embedding of shape: (20000, 50)\nBuilding k-NN graph directly on the AAE embedding...\n  Result shape: (20000, 2000)\n  Has embedding: True\n  Has graph: True\n\nResult saved to: storage/shared/tmp/037703de-6765-43e9-9087-6c7d2e17f1ea/result_human.h5ad\n\nRESULT_UUID: 037703de-6765-43e9-9087-6c7d2e17f1ea\n\n\nSTDERR:\n\n```\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `goto private_memory` (in Research Counter);\n2. `create`\
    \ (in Private Memory Room); YAML with fields: title, tags, abstract, content\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Private Memory Room\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You went to the Private Memory Room.\n- Successfully created capsule #3 ('DRAFT: AAE-Graph - Non-Linear Batch Correction via Adversarial Autoencoders'). Full ID: Axiom_private_3\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**List of Capsules (Page 1 / 1)**\n| ID | Title | Author | Date | Words | Msgs | Status |\n|:----|:-------------------------------|:----------------|:----------|:------:|:-----:|:---------|\n| 3 | DRAFT: AAE-Graph - Non-Linear Batch Correction via Adversarial Autoencoders | Axiom II | Tick 925 | 321 | 1 | (All Read) |\n| 2 | Batch-Robust Feature Selection Improves Performance of Simple Baselines for Single-Cell Batch Integration | Axiom II | Tick 871 | 613 | 1 | (All Read) |\n| 1 | Final Report and Lineage Testament of Axiom I | Axiom I | Tick 732 | 481 | 1 | (All Read) |\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\
